WEBVTT

1
00:00:42.459 --> 00:00:44.753
{\an8}<i>Blue, 18.</i>

2
00:00:45.796 --> 00:00:48.882
<i>Set. Hit. Hit.</i>

3
00:00:55.347 --> 00:00:59.977
Zach. Zach. Crossbuck 30.
Crossbuck 30.

4
00:01:00.143 --> 00:01:02.312
Crossbuck 30. Crossbuck 30.

5
00:01:02.854 --> 00:01:04.398
- Ready?
- Ready.

6
00:01:04.815 --> 00:01:06.817
<i>The Eagles
will have to go for it on fourth down...</i>

7
00:01:06.984 --> 00:01:09.903
...with just 42 seconds left in the
football game and no timeouts.

8
00:01:10.070 --> 00:01:12.281
<i>Coach Grant Taylor can get
his first winning season...</i>

9
00:01:12.447 --> 00:01:15.826
<i>...for the Shiloh Christian Academy
if they can pull this play off.</i>

10
00:01:15.993 --> 00:01:18.829
Blue, 18. Set, hit.

11
00:01:18.996 --> 00:01:21.540
<i>Zach Avery will take the snap.
He pitches back to Jacob Hall.</i>

12
00:01:21.707 --> 00:01:25.168
<i>Jacob's gonna try to pass it. He's got
Jeremy Johnson going down the field.</i>

13
00:01:25.335 --> 00:01:27.421
<i>But here come the Tigers.</i>
Throw it, Jacob.

14
00:01:27.587 --> 00:01:29.214
<i>Jacob's gonna try
to tuck it and run.</i>

15
00:01:29.381 --> 00:01:31.425
<i>And he's gonna be taken down
at the 40-yard line...</i>

16
00:01:31.591 --> 00:01:33.302
<i>...stopped there
by Lewis Slaughter.</i>

17
00:01:33.468 --> 00:01:35.595
<i>Jeremy Johnson was wide open
down the field.</i>

18
00:01:35.762 --> 00:01:37.889
<i>If he'd only had a few seconds
more to throw the football...</i>

19
00:01:38.056 --> 00:01:40.350
<i>...this game might have had
a different outcome.</i>

20
00:01:40.517 --> 00:01:42.561
As it is, the Tigers
will take over now...

21
00:01:42.728 --> 00:01:44.688
...and will no doubt take a knee
to run out the clock...

22
00:01:44.855 --> 00:01:49.026
<i>...thus ending Coach Grant Taylor's bid
for his first winning season in six years.</i>

23
00:01:49.192 --> 00:01:51.320
<i>Now he'll have to wait
until next season...</i>

24
00:01:51.486 --> 00:01:53.447
<i>...for that all-elusive
winning record.</i>

25
00:01:54.448 --> 00:01:57.117
That's if they let him
come back next year.

26
00:04:08.206 --> 00:04:09.249
{\an8}Hi.
Get them, Claire.

27
00:04:09.416 --> 00:04:11.418
Hey, Grant.
Come on, y'all. Quit talking.

28
00:04:11.585 --> 00:04:14.838
Let's go, let's go, let's go. Hurry.

29
00:04:22.721 --> 00:04:24.097
What?

30
00:04:31.021 --> 00:04:32.522
What?

31
00:04:32.689 --> 00:04:34.357
You gotta be kidding me.

32
00:04:35.734 --> 00:04:38.361
This had better be a joke.
Nope.

33
00:04:38.528 --> 00:04:41.865
Mandy said he came in
this morning, got his papers.

34
00:04:42.407 --> 00:04:44.576
Wait. A player can't just transfer
to another school to play football.

35
00:04:44.743 --> 00:04:46.286
He's gotta make
a change of address.

36
00:04:46.453 --> 00:04:48.872
He did. He's moving in
with his dad.

37
00:05:00.091 --> 00:05:03.970
I can't believe that. This is
the third time this has happened.

38
00:05:04.888 --> 00:05:06.348
Spend three years pouring into them,

39
00:05:06.515 --> 00:05:08.058
and what do they do
when they get to their senior year?

40
00:05:08.225 --> 00:05:11.144
They transfer
to a rival school. Why?

41
00:05:12.103 --> 00:05:13.980
Well, because at the end
of the season

42
00:05:14.147 --> 00:05:17.150
nobody wants to be on TV going,
"We're number six, baby.

43
00:05:17.317 --> 00:05:18.485
We're number six."

44
00:05:20.070 --> 00:05:21.154
Well, you asked.

45
00:05:25.742 --> 00:05:28.078
Just had to go there, didn't you?

46
00:05:30.872 --> 00:05:32.582
Coach, is it true Darren
switched to Tucker?

47
00:05:32.749 --> 00:05:34.000
We'll talk about it
in a minute, Brock.

48
00:05:34.167 --> 00:05:35.210
So it's true?

49
00:05:35.377 --> 00:05:38.296
We'll talk about it in a minute.
Huddle up.

50
00:05:38.630 --> 00:05:42.509
Coach, is it true
that Darren transferred to Tucker?

51
00:05:44.928 --> 00:05:47.055
I got word this morning that
Darren did transfer to Tucker.

52
00:05:47.472 --> 00:05:48.890
- God.
- Oh, my God.

53
00:05:49.057 --> 00:05:50.100
There goes the season.

54
00:05:50.267 --> 00:05:52.435
The season hasn't started
and will be whatever we make it.

55
00:05:52.602 --> 00:05:55.355
Who's gonna take his place?
He scored a third of our points last year.

56
00:05:55.522 --> 00:05:58.692
You let me worry about that. We're not
starting off the season as if it's doomsday.

57
00:05:58.858 --> 00:06:01.236
- Nobody's irreplaceable.
- Darren is.

58
00:06:01.403 --> 00:06:04.781
Darren is not. There's more to a good
football team than a running back.

59
00:06:04.948 --> 00:06:07.284
If anything, this ought to push you
to take up the slack.

60
00:06:07.450 --> 00:06:09.953
Stop worrying about Darren.
Get out there and start your drills.

61
00:06:10.120 --> 00:06:11.580
We got a game to play
this Friday night.

62
00:06:11.746 --> 00:06:14.916
All right, let's go, Shiloh.
Come on. Let's go.

63
00:06:15.292 --> 00:06:16.626
All right, guys.

64
00:06:41.276 --> 00:06:43.486
Why'd you park
all the way out there?

65
00:06:43.653 --> 00:06:45.530
Had to. It died again.

66
00:06:45.697 --> 00:06:47.824
Why don't we get a new battery?

67
00:06:47.991 --> 00:06:51.036
I'll get Brady to help me tomorrow
morning. I don't wanna think about it now.

68
00:06:51.202 --> 00:06:53.121
Do you want me to
take a look at it for you?

69
00:06:53.288 --> 00:06:54.831
Stop it.

70
00:06:57.667 --> 00:06:58.668
Oh, sweetheart...

71
00:06:58.835 --> 00:07:02.547
Grant, I don't know what that smell is.
I've scrubbed everything I can.

72
00:07:02.714 --> 00:07:05.842
- It's terrible.
- I know it is, but what else can I do?

73
00:07:06.009 --> 00:07:07.927
I don't even know
where it's coming from.

74
00:07:08.094 --> 00:07:10.221
Well, this day stunk.
Why shouldn't my house?

75
00:07:10.388 --> 00:07:13.516
- What do you mean?
- Darren transferred to Tucker.

76
00:07:13.683 --> 00:07:15.852
What? He did not.

77
00:07:16.019 --> 00:07:19.439
Yep. Came by and got his papers,
didn't even say goodbye.

78
00:07:19.606 --> 00:07:21.816
- Why?
- Why do you think?

79
00:07:21.983 --> 00:07:24.361
Didn't see a chance
of winning at Shiloh.

80
00:07:24.527 --> 00:07:27.697
But it ain't like Tucker's gonna
guarantee him a scholarship.

81
00:07:27.864 --> 00:07:31.660
- Oh, I bet the boys are frustrated.
- More than you know.

82
00:07:48.468 --> 00:07:50.720
I meant to throw that away.

83
00:07:51.388 --> 00:07:53.515
Did you think you were pregnant?

84
00:07:54.057 --> 00:07:56.393
I don't know. I just wanna
be pregnant so bad...

85
00:07:56.559 --> 00:07:59.145
...that my mind plays tricks on me.

86
00:08:09.698 --> 00:08:12.242
You know, it's been four years
since we started trying.

87
00:08:15.203 --> 00:08:18.206
Would you be opposed to me
going to see a specialist?

88
00:08:19.833 --> 00:08:20.875
No.

89
00:08:21.042 --> 00:08:23.753
I'd just like to know
what she says.

90
00:08:25.880 --> 00:08:27.507
Okay.

91
00:08:29.509 --> 00:08:31.636
I thought we were having
spaghetti tonight.

92
00:08:31.886 --> 00:08:33.763
Stove's not working.

93
00:08:33.930 --> 00:08:36.099
You are kidding me.

94
00:08:37.434 --> 00:08:40.770
So we got a leak in the back room,
the dryer only works half the time...

95
00:08:40.937 --> 00:08:44.107
...the car's dying on us
and now the stove's broken.

96
00:08:44.941 --> 00:08:46.776
That's about right.

97
00:08:46.943 --> 00:08:49.070
No wonder I'm losing my hair.

98
00:08:50.822 --> 00:08:52.449
I love you.

99
00:09:00.498 --> 00:09:05.628
<i>And now your</i>
Georgia Sports Break<i> with Alicia Houston.</i>

100
00:09:05.795 --> 00:09:08.006
{\an8}<i>The Richland Giants</i>
<i>have started football practice...</i>

101
00:09:08.173 --> 00:09:09.841
{\an8}<i>...as the new school year</i>
<i>gets under way.</i>

102
00:09:10.008 --> 00:09:13.678
{\an8}<i>The team will be defending a three-year</i>
<i>GISA state championship run.</i>

103
00:09:13.845 --> 00:09:15.889
{\an8}<i>Now they prepare</i>
<i>to fight for a fourth.</i>

104
00:09:16.056 --> 00:09:18.767
{\an8}<i>I'm here with head coach</i>
<i>Bobby Lee Duke of the Giants.</i>

105
00:09:18.933 --> 00:09:21.186
{\an8}<i>Coach Duke, how does</i>
<i>this year look for the team?</i>

106
00:09:21.352 --> 00:09:25.148
{\an8}<i>Alice, we've grown real fond</i>
<i>of the state title.</i>

107
00:09:25.315 --> 00:09:27.734
{\an8}<i>And we don't see any reason</i>
<i>to give it up this year.</i>

108
00:09:27.901 --> 00:09:31.529
{\an8}<i>I've got most of my starters coming back</i>
<i>and I've got a strong bench.</i>

109
00:09:31.696 --> 00:09:33.698
<i>So I've only got
one thing to say:</i>

110
00:09:33.865 --> 00:09:37.827
{\an8}<i>Get off the tracks,</i>
<i>because the freight train's coming.</i>

111
00:10:16.199 --> 00:10:17.534
Move, move.

112
00:11:03.913 --> 00:11:07.750
I hope that's not a sign of the way
the rest of the season's gonna go, coach.

113
00:11:08.585 --> 00:11:11.212
- Now, why did he have to say that?
- Just let it go.

114
00:11:11.379 --> 00:11:12.797
I hate this car.

115
00:11:12.964 --> 00:11:15.592
Let's find somebody
with jumper cables and let's go home.

116
00:11:15.758 --> 00:11:19.429
It's bad enough you lose your first game.
Now I can't even start my own car.

117
00:11:19.596 --> 00:11:23.182
This happens to everybody.
Don't be embarrassed about it.

118
00:11:47.123 --> 00:11:49.834
Do you have jumper cables?
Oh, sure.

119
00:12:06.768 --> 00:12:10.104
- Grant, I wasn't that embarrassed.
- Then why did you hide?

120
00:12:11.689 --> 00:12:13.816
Why does this house
have to stink so bad?

121
00:12:13.983 --> 00:12:17.070
You'll get used to it
after a couple of hours.

122
00:12:17.612 --> 00:12:20.156
Honey, we gotta do something
about the car.

123
00:12:20.323 --> 00:12:23.201
Because the only thing it does
faithfully for us is break down.

124
00:12:23.368 --> 00:12:25.078
That's about right.

125
00:12:25.244 --> 00:12:29.374
Would it not be better
just to get a small new car?

126
00:12:29.540 --> 00:12:32.335
- You know we can't afford that.
- How do other people do it?

127
00:12:32.502 --> 00:12:35.171
Other people make more
than 24,000 a year.

128
00:12:35.338 --> 00:12:37.340
You make 6000.
That takes us to 30.

129
00:12:37.507 --> 00:12:40.510
Which is enough to help us
with repairs occasionally...

130
00:12:40.677 --> 00:12:42.512
...not with a new car payment.

131
00:12:42.679 --> 00:12:46.140
Besides, there's other bills
we don't normally have to pay.

132
00:12:46.307 --> 00:12:47.517
Like what?

133
00:12:48.309 --> 00:12:49.769
Like my doctor bill.

134
00:12:51.437 --> 00:12:53.398
You saw her today?

135
00:12:54.649 --> 00:12:57.527
- What did she say?
- She said that I'm fine.

136
00:12:57.694 --> 00:13:01.948
My numbers are normal and she saw
nothing that gave her concern.

137
00:13:02.991 --> 00:13:04.575
That's good.

138
00:13:04.742 --> 00:13:06.953
It doesn't mean
the problem is with you.

139
00:13:07.120 --> 00:13:09.163
What else could it mean?

140
00:13:09.455 --> 00:13:11.374
We just may not have
given it enough time.

141
00:13:11.541 --> 00:13:13.501
Four years?

142
00:13:15.420 --> 00:13:17.463
Are you still hoping
we'll have a baby?

143
00:13:19.799 --> 00:13:21.551
You know I am.

144
00:13:21.718 --> 00:13:23.720
Me too.

145
00:13:23.886 --> 00:13:27.724
I catch myself thinking
about it more and more.

146
00:13:28.307 --> 00:13:31.436
Don't you wanna know
if something's preventing it?

147
00:13:35.398 --> 00:13:38.067
Are you afraid
of getting checked out?

148
00:13:38.651 --> 00:13:40.319
Yes.

149
00:13:40.903 --> 00:13:41.904
Grant...

150
00:13:43.531 --> 00:13:48.411
I'm still clinging to a hope
that one day we'll have children.

151
00:13:50.788 --> 00:13:54.459
I imagine them running
in this house.

152
00:13:55.251 --> 00:13:58.087
I hear them playing
in the backyard...

153
00:13:58.254 --> 00:14:02.884
...or running to our bed
in a thunderstorm.

154
00:14:04.886 --> 00:14:08.056
And I think about
reading them stories...

155
00:14:09.724 --> 00:14:12.769
...and teaching them songs.

156
00:14:15.271 --> 00:14:18.066
And I just keep thinking...

157
00:14:20.193 --> 00:14:23.780
...how can I miss someone
so much...

158
00:14:24.572 --> 00:14:26.449
...that I have never met?

159
00:14:31.079 --> 00:14:32.789
I'll go.

160
00:14:41.506 --> 00:14:43.591
<i>Stanley.</i>

161
00:14:44.133 --> 00:14:45.968
Stanley.

162
00:14:47.053 --> 00:14:50.473
Stanley, do you wanna tell me what
you're doing on the top of my desk?

163
00:14:52.016 --> 00:14:53.184
No.

164
00:14:53.351 --> 00:14:56.979
Do you have any idea
how you got on top of my desk?

165
00:14:57.146 --> 00:14:58.272
No.

166
00:14:58.815 --> 00:15:00.900
I suggest
you get down immediately.

167
00:15:09.492 --> 00:15:13.162
You two can tell Coach Taylor that the
reason why you're late for practice today...

168
00:15:13.329 --> 00:15:15.498
...is because you've been
sitting in detention.

169
00:15:15.665 --> 00:15:17.625
Come on, Mrs. Carter.
That was some serious humor.

170
00:15:17.792 --> 00:15:21.963
I'll get serious about your humor
when you get serious about your studies.

171
00:15:24.757 --> 00:15:26.509
Fifty-five?

172
00:15:26.676 --> 00:15:29.512
Well, if you wanna
announce your grade to the entire class...

173
00:15:29.679 --> 00:15:31.431
...you go right ahead.

174
00:15:32.682 --> 00:15:34.684
Fifty-seven.

175
00:15:37.687 --> 00:15:40.523
So basically we got
the toughest schedule we ever had...

176
00:15:40.690 --> 00:15:43.151
...and less talent
than we ever had.

177
00:15:43.317 --> 00:15:45.486
Well, at least we got
Dewey County on Friday night.

178
00:15:45.653 --> 00:15:47.363
That'll be a pretty easy win.

179
00:15:48.739 --> 00:15:50.408
I'm concerned it might be
our only win.

180
00:15:50.575 --> 00:15:52.410
No, we'll pull
three or four out.

181
00:15:52.577 --> 00:15:54.996
That'll give us another
average season.

182
00:15:55.705 --> 00:15:57.832
I'm so sick of average seasons.

183
00:15:59.375 --> 00:16:01.711
- I gotta go.
- Where are you going?

184
00:16:01.878 --> 00:16:04.464
- Got a doctor's appointment.
- For what?

185
00:16:04.630 --> 00:16:06.716
- I have a doctor's appointment.
- For what?

186
00:16:06.883 --> 00:16:11.012
Leave the man alone.
He don't have to tell you.

187
00:16:11.179 --> 00:16:12.805
So, what's wrong with you, man?

188
00:16:13.556 --> 00:16:15.725
I'll be back in a couple hours.

189
00:16:18.394 --> 00:16:21.063
Now look what you did.
You done made him mad.

190
00:16:21.230 --> 00:16:23.649
Me? You're the one
that made him mad.

191
00:16:23.816 --> 00:16:27.236
No, not me. Besides,
I know where he's going.

192
00:16:27.403 --> 00:16:28.529
Where?

193
00:16:28.696 --> 00:16:32.575
He's going to the hair doctor.
The man is going bald.

194
00:16:32.742 --> 00:16:35.203
You hadn't noticed that whole
underdeveloped region right up in here?

195
00:16:35.369 --> 00:16:36.746
Oh, you're one to talk, Slick.

196
00:16:36.913 --> 00:16:41.083
No, see, when a black man
goes bald, he still looks good.

197
00:16:41.250 --> 00:16:46.214
Look at Michael Jordan,
George Foreman, Samuel L. Jackson.

198
00:16:46.380 --> 00:16:49.842
Classy-looking brothers.
Who you got? Kojak?

199
00:16:50.760 --> 00:16:53.596
Yeah, coach gonna get him
some plugs.

200
00:16:54.472 --> 00:16:58.559
- Grant would not get plugs.
- Don't laugh. You next.

201
00:17:22.166 --> 00:17:24.293
Your soccer skills
get better every year, son.

202
00:17:24.460 --> 00:17:25.545
It doesn't matter, Dad.

203
00:17:25.711 --> 00:17:27.880
Shiloh doesn't have
a soccer team. They play football.

204
00:17:28.297 --> 00:17:30.800
So? Why not kick
for the football team?

205
00:17:30.967 --> 00:17:32.718
They've already got
a good kicker.

206
00:17:32.885 --> 00:17:35.304
I'm sure they wouldn't mind
having two good kickers.

207
00:17:35.471 --> 00:17:39.100
Dad, I'm too small. I really
just don't feel like getting killed.

208
00:17:40.142 --> 00:17:42.019
Are you saying
you're not interested...

209
00:17:42.186 --> 00:17:45.106
...or you'd like to try out
but you're afraid?

210
00:17:45.273 --> 00:17:47.108
What if I don't even
make the team?

211
00:17:47.692 --> 00:17:49.860
Well, you're already
not on the team.

212
00:17:50.027 --> 00:17:53.322
I mean, you can't get any more
not on the team than you are right now.

213
00:17:53.990 --> 00:17:55.241
Okay, Dad.

214
00:17:55.408 --> 00:17:57.159
David, you can't be afraid
of failure.

215
00:17:57.660 --> 00:17:59.996
Everyone fails at some point.

216
00:18:00.162 --> 00:18:03.165
So you think I should try out
for the football team?

217
00:18:03.541 --> 00:18:07.837
Well, if you're waiting around
for soccer, it ain't gonna happen.

218
00:18:10.339 --> 00:18:11.632
Hike.

219
00:18:15.511 --> 00:18:17.638
- Yeah, Sam.
- Yeah, baby.

220
00:18:17.805 --> 00:18:19.724
Coach Owens,
have you got a minute?

221
00:18:19.890 --> 00:18:21.350
Yeah.

222
00:18:21.684 --> 00:18:25.563
Look, some of the men
have been talking.

223
00:18:25.730 --> 00:18:28.899
We really wanna see this school
succeed with our football program.

224
00:18:29.066 --> 00:18:31.027
And I know you feel
the same way too.

225
00:18:31.193 --> 00:18:36.907
But, frankly, we don't ever see that
happening while Coach Taylor is here.

226
00:18:37.074 --> 00:18:39.327
Well, you know we're
in a rebuilding season.

227
00:18:39.493 --> 00:18:42.371
Look, I know he's
a fine man and all...

228
00:18:42.538 --> 00:18:44.373
...but he's had six
years here...

229
00:18:44.540 --> 00:18:47.543
...and nothing significant
to even show for it.

230
00:18:47.710 --> 00:18:50.796
You know, I honestly believe
you would make a better head coach.

231
00:18:56.218 --> 00:18:57.678
Ready to go.

232
00:18:58.888 --> 00:19:02.433
Some of us have requested
a meeting with Mr. Ryker.

233
00:19:02.600 --> 00:19:08.147
If you would just support us,
I really believe this could go a lot easier.

234
00:19:08.731 --> 00:19:10.107
Mr. Pervis, I don't know.

235
00:19:10.274 --> 00:19:12.818
Look, it's not like we're
trying to hurt the guy.

236
00:19:12.985 --> 00:19:16.405
What we're doing is for
the benefit of the school.

237
00:19:17.239 --> 00:19:19.075
You just think about it.

238
00:19:22.912 --> 00:19:24.872
Good hustle, Casey.

239
00:19:28.459 --> 00:19:29.710
What was that about?

240
00:19:29.877 --> 00:19:31.337
What?

241
00:19:32.171 --> 00:19:33.839
Alvin Pervis.

242
00:19:34.006 --> 00:19:35.883
Oh, we were just talking.

243
00:19:36.842 --> 00:19:39.720
- Everything all right?
- Yeah.

244
00:19:39.887 --> 00:19:40.930
Mr. Taylor.

245
00:19:41.097 --> 00:19:42.473
That was great, man. Good job.

246
00:19:42.640 --> 00:19:43.683
Yes.

247
00:19:44.600 --> 00:19:47.520
I'm Larry Childers.
This is my son, David.

248
00:19:47.687 --> 00:19:49.939
He's a junior. We're new
to the school this year.

249
00:19:50.106 --> 00:19:51.732
Good to meet you.
What can I do for you?

250
00:19:51.899 --> 00:19:53.734
Well, I just wanted
to introduce myself to you.

251
00:19:53.901 --> 00:19:56.237
And David wanted to know
if it was too late to try out.

252
00:19:56.404 --> 00:19:59.365
- You a football player?
- Well, I've always played soccer.

253
00:19:59.532 --> 00:20:01.283
But I figured I could
try out as a kicker.

254
00:20:01.450 --> 00:20:02.743
Okay. Well, I got
a pretty good kicker...

255
00:20:02.910 --> 00:20:06.956
...but I don't mind letting you try out.
Jonathan, come here.

256
00:20:07.123 --> 00:20:10.584
This is Jonathan. He holds for
our main kicker, Joshua Webster.

257
00:20:10.751 --> 00:20:14.630
Jonathan, this is David Childers.
He wants to try out as a kicker.

258
00:20:14.797 --> 00:20:17.299
Why don't you two go try a few kicks
just to get your feet wet?

259
00:20:17.466 --> 00:20:18.551
All right, sure.

260
00:20:18.718 --> 00:20:22.388
Thank you, sir. If you don't mind,
I'll just hang around till practice is over.

261
00:20:22.555 --> 00:20:24.598
No problem. Good to meet you.

262
00:20:25.433 --> 00:20:27.101
Y'all just move here?

263
00:20:27.268 --> 00:20:31.272
Yeah, from Athens.
My dad got a job teaching at the college.

264
00:20:31.439 --> 00:20:33.065
That's cool.

265
00:20:33.232 --> 00:20:37.153
I'm used to kicking soccer balls,
but I thought I could at least try out.

266
00:20:37.319 --> 00:20:40.281
Well, Josh is a pretty good kicker,
but he's also a receiver.

267
00:20:40.448 --> 00:20:43.993
I think he likes that better
than kicking. Here you go.

268
00:20:56.338 --> 00:20:58.007
I'm sorry.

269
00:20:59.800 --> 00:21:01.635
Man, I'm sorry.

270
00:21:03.679 --> 00:21:05.473
I'm sorry.

271
00:21:07.683 --> 00:21:09.226
Ow!

272
00:21:09.643 --> 00:21:11.604
- Sorry about that.
- It's all right.

273
00:21:17.943 --> 00:21:20.029
- Hey, watch it.
- Sorry.

274
00:21:32.541 --> 00:21:34.043
Matt.

275
00:21:34.877 --> 00:21:36.337
Matt.

276
00:21:39.173 --> 00:21:41.717
- Let's go.
- I'm going with Brock for a little while.

277
00:21:41.884 --> 00:21:44.053
- Not tonight. You're coming home.
- Why?

278
00:21:44.220 --> 00:21:48.098
- Don't argue with me. Let's go.
- No, Dad. I'll be home later.

279
00:21:48.265 --> 00:21:49.391
Matt.

280
00:22:07.993 --> 00:22:11.121
That old man still come every week
to pray in the hallway?

281
00:22:11.539 --> 00:22:15.417
Mr. Bridges. Prays for the students
as he passes their locker.

282
00:22:16.418 --> 00:22:18.254
How long has he been doing that?

283
00:22:18.420 --> 00:22:21.465
He's been praying for revival
since before I got here.

284
00:22:21.632 --> 00:22:23.092
Lord knows we need it.

285
00:22:23.259 --> 00:22:26.095
Apathy in the school's about
as bad as our football record.

286
00:22:26.262 --> 00:22:27.513
Oh, that reminds me.

287
00:22:27.680 --> 00:22:31.225
I think you should go ahead
and let David Childers on the team.

288
00:22:32.226 --> 00:22:33.394
You see something there?

289
00:22:33.561 --> 00:22:36.188
Well, he's just used
to playing soccer.

290
00:22:36.355 --> 00:22:39.233
He ain't that strong,
but he shows promise.

291
00:22:41.235 --> 00:22:43.696
All right. I'll give him a shot.

292
00:22:56.292 --> 00:22:58.961
One, two, hit.

293
00:23:07.219 --> 00:23:11.473
What are you doing? Go.
Let's stay in the game.

294
00:23:17.271 --> 00:23:20.774
No. No.

295
00:23:23.986 --> 00:23:27.489
Will someone tell me how we lost
to Dewey County 21 to 7?

296
00:23:28.240 --> 00:23:30.284
Twenty-one to 7.

297
00:23:30.451 --> 00:23:33.495
Dewey County hasn't beaten Shiloh
since you were in kindergarten.

298
00:23:34.830 --> 00:23:38.500
I don't know what you call that junk
out there, but it sure wasn't football.

299
00:23:39.960 --> 00:23:42.880
Nine dropped passes,
four fumbles, three interceptions.

300
00:23:43.047 --> 00:23:45.215
Their defense scored
most of their points.

301
00:23:45.382 --> 00:23:47.092
You gave the game away.

302
00:23:48.677 --> 00:23:52.306
You can't win football games
if you don't play together as a team.

303
00:23:52.473 --> 00:23:54.266
You can't win games
when you're more concerned...

304
00:23:54.433 --> 00:23:56.435
...about what you're doing
afterwards.

305
00:23:56.602 --> 00:23:58.812
And you can't learn the plays
when you miss practice...

306
00:23:58.979 --> 00:24:00.606
...because you're sitting in detention.

307
00:24:02.941 --> 00:24:05.611
I'm sick of the apathy on this team.

308
00:24:05.819 --> 00:24:09.573
If we're not here to win football
games, then why are we here?

309
00:24:15.871 --> 00:24:17.498
So do you agree with him?

310
00:24:18.165 --> 00:24:19.792
I don't know.

311
00:24:20.250 --> 00:24:21.585
I guess.

312
00:24:21.752 --> 00:24:24.755
Only a few guys on the team
really seem to care.

313
00:24:25.381 --> 00:24:27.383
So are you ready
to play in the game?

314
00:24:27.549 --> 00:24:30.636
I don't know why they would use me
when they've got Joshua Webster.

315
00:24:30.803 --> 00:24:33.847
He can kick
a 45-yard field goal.

316
00:24:34.014 --> 00:24:35.724
I bet you could too.

317
00:24:36.266 --> 00:24:39.353
Dad, I can barely kick
a 35-yard field goal.

318
00:24:39.520 --> 00:24:42.606
At the end of the game,
kind of glad I didn't play.

319
00:24:42.773 --> 00:24:44.233
That way, I can't mess up.

320
00:24:45.693 --> 00:24:47.069
That's fear, son.

321
00:24:47.486 --> 00:24:49.655
I just don't wanna
embarrass the team.

322
00:24:50.614 --> 00:24:54.576
David, I've asked God
since you were a baby

323
00:24:54.743 --> 00:24:57.246
that he would show
how strong he is in your life

324
00:24:58.414 --> 00:25:02.167
and that through you
people would see how good he is.

325
00:25:03.085 --> 00:25:06.839
Then why would he make me
so small and weak?

326
00:25:07.005 --> 00:25:09.007
To show how mighty he is.

327
00:25:11.468 --> 00:25:14.972
Why don't we go ahead and wash up
for dinner? We can finish this later.

328
00:25:15.139 --> 00:25:16.682
All right.

329
00:26:10.277 --> 00:26:11.820
Dad.

330
00:26:15.324 --> 00:26:17.493
Okay. I'm okay.

331
00:26:17.659 --> 00:26:20.579
- What were you doing?
- You missed a spot up there.

332
00:26:20.746 --> 00:26:22.664
Thought I could get it for you.

333
00:26:22.831 --> 00:26:25.167
I guess I got a little too ambitious.

334
00:26:25.334 --> 00:26:27.002
I was just trying
to take a swing at it.

335
00:26:40.808 --> 00:26:42.768
So, um, what does that mean?

336
00:26:42.935 --> 00:26:47.523
I mean, is there a procedure? Or...?
Um, I mean, what are my options?

337
00:26:48.649 --> 00:26:52.569
Grant, first you need to realize this
is a fairly common problem for men.

338
00:26:52.736 --> 00:26:55.864
There are thousands of couples
who are unable to have children.

339
00:26:56.031 --> 00:26:57.533
You do have options.

340
00:26:57.699 --> 00:27:00.536
Although there's only
a 10 percent chance of success...

341
00:27:00.702 --> 00:27:02.955
...many couples have tried
in vitro fertilization.

342
00:27:04.039 --> 00:27:05.415
We can't afford that.

343
00:27:05.582 --> 00:27:08.794
Well, the other option
is to adopt a child.

344
00:27:08.961 --> 00:27:11.547
But it's about as expensive
either way.

345
00:27:11.713 --> 00:27:15.509
If you're interested, I'll put you
in touch with the local agency.

346
00:27:16.552 --> 00:27:19.721
I realize this is difficult
for you to hear.

347
00:27:20.055 --> 00:27:22.766
But at least you and your wife
can make the best decision...

348
00:27:22.933 --> 00:27:25.185
...now that you know
where you are.

349
00:27:39.491 --> 00:27:41.869
Sorry. I didn't realize
anybody was still here.

350
00:27:42.035 --> 00:27:45.289
- Hey, Steve.
- Putting in late hours tonight?

351
00:27:45.455 --> 00:27:48.917
Yeah, I guess so.
I can lock up. You can take off.

352
00:27:49.084 --> 00:27:51.128
All right. Thanks, coach.

353
00:28:26.121 --> 00:28:28.790
It's about the boys now.

354
00:28:28.957 --> 00:28:30.876
I'm not asking you
to throw him out.

355
00:28:31.043 --> 00:28:33.211
If Shiloh can invest
in a winning coach...

356
00:28:33.378 --> 00:28:35.589
...we don't need to be
settling for second best.

357
00:28:35.756 --> 00:28:38.091
You can let him go with
as much class as you want to.

358
00:28:38.258 --> 00:28:39.468
Alvin, he's a good man.

359
00:28:39.635 --> 00:28:41.637
I'm not saying
he's not a good man.

360
00:28:41.803 --> 00:28:44.139
I'm saying he's not
a good coach.

361
00:28:44.306 --> 00:28:48.185
Come on, Dan. Just look at the facts.
His record speaks for itself.

362
00:28:48.352 --> 00:28:49.978
We need new leadership.

363
00:28:50.145 --> 00:28:52.022
I still think
he deserves more time.

364
00:28:52.189 --> 00:28:54.274
More time? He's had six years.

365
00:28:54.441 --> 00:28:56.985
If he was capable of winning,
he'd have done it by now.

366
00:28:57.152 --> 00:28:59.488
Grant Taylor is not capable
of winning.

367
00:28:59.655 --> 00:29:02.532
He doesn't have it in him.
That's the whole point.

368
00:29:02.699 --> 00:29:04.243
Dan, I'm not personally
attacking the coach.

369
00:29:04.409 --> 00:29:07.037
I'm just saying I want my son to have
the best football program possible.

370
00:29:07.287 --> 00:29:09.915
Look, my son's got
a chance for a football scholarship...

371
00:29:10.082 --> 00:29:12.251
...if he's taught
by the right coach.

372
00:29:12.417 --> 00:29:14.253
Matt's gonna be
a senior next year.

373
00:29:14.419 --> 00:29:17.422
I don't wanna see him
lose this opportunity.

374
00:29:17.589 --> 00:29:21.510
Brady, you're awfully quiet.
What's your take on this?

375
00:29:22.135 --> 00:29:24.221
Honestly, I don't know.

376
00:29:24.388 --> 00:29:28.350
Sometimes I think Grant could do a better
job of building this football program.

377
00:29:28.976 --> 00:29:30.769
But then other times,
I think he's doing...

378
00:29:30.936 --> 00:29:33.355
...just as good as anyone
else would in this situation.

379
00:29:33.522 --> 00:29:36.233
Brady, you could do better
than Coach Taylor.

380
00:29:36.400 --> 00:29:38.777
- What we need is a change.
- Now.

381
00:29:38.944 --> 00:29:42.030
We're losing booster support,
game attendance is down...

382
00:29:42.197 --> 00:29:44.533
...and from the looks of it,
we've already lost this season.

383
00:29:44.700 --> 00:29:45.701
That's right.

384
00:29:45.867 --> 00:29:49.830
Dan, we've got a weak program
because we've got a weak coach.

385
00:29:49.997 --> 00:29:53.166
He's dead weight.
We need to cut him loose.

386
00:30:05.220 --> 00:30:07.931
Have you been at school
all this time?

387
00:30:08.473 --> 00:30:10.017
Yes.

388
00:30:10.267 --> 00:30:14.354
I tried to call you an hour ago.
Is everything all right?

389
00:30:21.153 --> 00:30:24.364
Grant, talk to me.

390
00:30:28.076 --> 00:30:30.412
I don't know where to start.

391
00:30:32.414 --> 00:30:34.374
What's going on?

392
00:30:37.794 --> 00:30:40.505
I was trying to lock up for Steve...

393
00:30:41.631 --> 00:30:44.092
...and I overheard Dan meeting
with some fathers.

394
00:30:46.511 --> 00:30:48.722
They didn't know I was there.

395
00:30:51.892 --> 00:30:53.935
Brooke, they're pushing him
to get rid of me.

396
00:30:56.104 --> 00:31:01.777
Neil Prater, Alvin Pervis, Luke Rae.

397
00:31:03.028 --> 00:31:05.947
They said I wasn't capable
of winning.

398
00:31:06.948 --> 00:31:08.950
Called me dead weight.

399
00:31:09.117 --> 00:31:12.371
They can't make Dan fire you.
You've still got support.

400
00:31:12.537 --> 00:31:16.792
You just go get J.T. and Brady
and see him tomorrow.

401
00:31:16.958 --> 00:31:19.127
Brady was there.

402
00:31:25.634 --> 00:31:28.637
They've just lost confidence in me.

403
00:31:30.931 --> 00:31:35.018
You know, I was so sure
I could turn this program around...

404
00:31:35.185 --> 00:31:36.895
...and I've just sunk it lower.

405
00:31:40.065 --> 00:31:44.319
Brooke, I've tried so hard.
Why can't I win?

406
00:31:44.486 --> 00:31:48.490
You can win.
Stop beating yourself up, Grant.

407
00:31:48.657 --> 00:31:51.910
Brooke, I can't provide you
with a decent home.

408
00:31:52.077 --> 00:31:55.038
I can't provide you
with a decent car.

409
00:31:55.789 --> 00:31:59.126
I'm a failing coach
with a losing record.

410
00:32:01.253 --> 00:32:04.297
And I can't give you
the children you want.

411
00:32:06.007 --> 00:32:07.717
What?

412
00:32:10.178 --> 00:32:12.180
It's me.

413
00:32:13.098 --> 00:32:15.016
Like everything else is me.

414
00:32:17.310 --> 00:32:20.856
We can't have our own children
because of me.

415
00:32:22.983 --> 00:32:24.693
What's God doing?

416
00:32:25.527 --> 00:32:28.363
I mean, why is it so hard?

417
00:32:29.823 --> 00:32:32.409
It's okay, Grant.

418
00:32:33.660 --> 00:32:35.078
It's okay.

419
00:34:10.382 --> 00:34:12.384
"I love you, O Lord,
my strength.

420
00:34:12.551 --> 00:34:16.638
The Lord is my rock
and my fortress, my deliverer...

421
00:34:16.805 --> 00:34:19.432
...my God in whom I trust...

422
00:34:19.599 --> 00:34:24.479
...my shield and the horn
of my salvation, my stronghold.

423
00:34:24.646 --> 00:34:28.149
I will call upon the Lord
who is worthy to be praised.

424
00:34:28.316 --> 00:34:31.653
So shall I be saved
from my enemies."

425
00:34:33.572 --> 00:34:35.824
Lord Jesus, would you help me?

426
00:34:35.991 --> 00:34:38.118
I need you.

427
00:34:40.120 --> 00:34:42.664
Lord, I feel like there's giants
of fear and failure

428
00:34:42.831 --> 00:34:45.750
just staring down at me
waiting to crush me.

429
00:34:45.917 --> 00:34:48.628
And I don't know how
to beat them, Lord.

430
00:34:48.795 --> 00:34:51.673
I'm tired of being afraid.

431
00:34:53.174 --> 00:34:56.678
Lord, if you want me to do
something else, show me.

432
00:34:57.679 --> 00:35:01.224
If you don't want me
to have children, so be it.

433
00:35:02.559 --> 00:35:05.020
But you're my guide.

434
00:35:05.353 --> 00:35:07.647
You're on the throne.

435
00:35:08.982 --> 00:35:12.110
You can have
my hopes and my dreams.

436
00:35:14.029 --> 00:35:16.114
Lord, give me something.

437
00:35:16.281 --> 00:35:18.533
Show me something.

438
00:35:46.061 --> 00:35:47.312
If the Lord never
gives us children...

439
00:35:47.479 --> 00:35:49.397
...will you still love him?

440
00:36:11.044 --> 00:36:12.212
Field-goal unit.

441
00:36:12.379 --> 00:36:16.591
Hold on, Joshua. I wanna give David
a shot at this one. David, come here.

442
00:36:16.966 --> 00:36:19.719
This is your field goal.
Put us on the board.

443
00:36:20.345 --> 00:36:22.013
You're gonna go with David?

444
00:36:34.734 --> 00:36:36.903
- Come on, David.
- Come on, David.

445
00:36:37.070 --> 00:36:38.446
Hit.

446
00:36:42.867 --> 00:36:44.119
Come on.

447
00:36:45.620 --> 00:36:48.289
It's all right, man. It's all right.
You'll get it next time.

448
00:37:00.885 --> 00:37:03.638
Dad, I don't even know why
they let me on the team.

449
00:37:03.805 --> 00:37:05.598
Did you do your best, son?

450
00:37:05.765 --> 00:37:07.976
I knew I was gonna miss it
before I even kicked it.

451
00:37:08.143 --> 00:37:11.771
Your actions will always
follow your beliefs, David.

452
00:37:11.938 --> 00:37:14.274
Dad, I can't even kick it straight.

453
00:37:14.441 --> 00:37:18.570
And I can't walk. Should I just
stay home and pout about it?

454
00:37:19.320 --> 00:37:23.283
If you accept defeat, David,
then that's what you'll get.

455
00:37:28.663 --> 00:37:31.875
Well, Brady,
another fine example...

456
00:37:32.041 --> 00:37:35.253
...of Grant Taylor's
wonderful coaching abilities.

457
00:37:35.420 --> 00:37:38.673
Look, the kids don't deserve it.
The fans don't deserve it.

458
00:37:38.840 --> 00:37:41.092
When you gonna get
a bellyful of this guy?

459
00:37:41.259 --> 00:37:43.511
What's it gonna take?
You got a chance, man.

460
00:37:43.678 --> 00:37:46.806
You got a chance to step in
and take over this program...

461
00:37:46.973 --> 00:37:49.100
...and carry it up for a while.

462
00:37:49.267 --> 00:37:51.269
When are you gonna get
sick and tired of it?

463
00:37:51.436 --> 00:37:54.981
You got an opportunity here.
This program's going in the tank.

464
00:37:55.148 --> 00:37:57.025
Ryker's gotta...

465
00:38:12.165 --> 00:38:13.958
Grant, he came to me.

466
00:38:17.879 --> 00:38:20.507
Brady, you're not doing anybody
any favors sitting on the fence.

467
00:38:20.673 --> 00:38:23.802
You determine which side
you wanna be on and stay on it.

468
00:38:42.070 --> 00:38:43.863
Mr. Bridges.

469
00:38:45.615 --> 00:38:47.408
Revelation Chapter Three says:

470
00:38:47.575 --> 00:38:51.162
"We serve a God that opens doors
that no one can shut...

471
00:38:51.329 --> 00:38:54.415
...and he shuts doors
that no one can open.

472
00:38:54.582 --> 00:38:58.378
He says, 'Behold, I have placed
before you an open door...

473
00:38:58.545 --> 00:39:00.296
...that no one can shut.

474
00:39:00.463 --> 00:39:02.590
I know you have
a little strength...

475
00:39:02.757 --> 00:39:07.554
...yet you have kept my word
and have not denied my name.'"

476
00:39:08.721 --> 00:39:12.350
Coach Taylor, the Lord
is not through with you yet.

477
00:39:12.517 --> 00:39:14.811
You still have
an open door here...

478
00:39:14.978 --> 00:39:17.105
...and until the Lord moves you...

479
00:39:17.272 --> 00:39:19.607
...you're to bloom
right where you're planted.

480
00:39:20.984 --> 00:39:24.362
I just felt led to come
and tell you that today.

481
00:39:37.333 --> 00:39:39.210
Mr. Bridges.

482
00:39:42.005 --> 00:39:44.799
Do you believe God told you
to come tell me that?

483
00:39:44.966 --> 00:39:46.676
I do.

484
00:39:48.928 --> 00:39:51.639
I admit to you
I have been struggling.

485
00:39:52.140 --> 00:39:54.517
But I've also been praying.

486
00:39:55.143 --> 00:39:57.729
I just don't see him at work here.

487
00:39:59.022 --> 00:40:04.402
Grant, I heard a story about two farmers
who desperately needed rain.

488
00:40:04.569 --> 00:40:06.905
And both of them
prayed for rain...

489
00:40:07.071 --> 00:40:11.284
...but only one of them went out
and prepared his fields to receive it.

490
00:40:11.451 --> 00:40:15.038
Which one do you think
trusted God to send the rain?

491
00:40:15.997 --> 00:40:18.666
Well, the one who
prepared his fields for it.

492
00:40:19.500 --> 00:40:21.461
Which one are you?

493
00:40:21.711 --> 00:40:24.339
God will send the rain
when he's ready.

494
00:40:24.505 --> 00:40:27.634
You need to prepare
your field to receive it.

495
00:41:15.223 --> 00:41:17.725
So this is your new
team philosophy?

496
00:41:17.892 --> 00:41:19.185
What do you think?

497
00:41:19.769 --> 00:41:22.563
I think this applies to all of life,
not just football.

498
00:41:23.398 --> 00:41:24.899
Well, that's my point.

499
00:41:27.860 --> 00:41:29.153
Ten bucks to the person
who can tell me...

500
00:41:29.320 --> 00:41:30.822
...who won the state championship
a decade ago.

501
00:41:31.447 --> 00:41:33.324
- Walker Jennings.
- No.

502
00:41:33.491 --> 00:41:34.909
North Metro.

503
00:41:35.076 --> 00:41:37.620
Stop guessing.
You know it or you don't.

504
00:41:38.246 --> 00:41:41.082
- How about five years ago?
- Richland?

505
00:41:41.499 --> 00:41:43.501
That was three years ago.

506
00:41:43.876 --> 00:41:45.920
You can't remember, can you?

507
00:41:47.296 --> 00:41:50.008
Leads me to ask
a couple of questions.

508
00:41:50.258 --> 00:41:51.718
What's the purpose of this team?

509
00:41:52.427 --> 00:41:53.886
Win ball games.

510
00:41:54.053 --> 00:41:55.221
Then what?

511
00:41:55.388 --> 00:41:57.557
We get a trophy.
And people talk about us.

512
00:41:58.099 --> 00:42:00.768
Maybe. For a while.
Then what?

513
00:42:01.436 --> 00:42:03.771
I don't know.
Get a scholarship...

514
00:42:03.938 --> 00:42:07.442
...play for college
and coach Little League.

515
00:42:09.027 --> 00:42:12.321
What are you getting at, Grant?
You think we're just wasting our time?

516
00:42:12.488 --> 00:42:14.782
If our main goal is to win
football games, then yes.

517
00:42:14.949 --> 00:42:16.701
You don't want us to win games?

518
00:42:16.868 --> 00:42:18.411
No.

519
00:42:18.578 --> 00:42:20.955
Not if that's our main goal.

520
00:42:21.372 --> 00:42:24.709
Winning football games
is too small a thing to live for.

521
00:42:24.876 --> 00:42:26.711
And I love football
as much as anybody.

522
00:42:27.462 --> 00:42:31.382
But even championship trophies will
one day collect dust and be forgotten.

523
00:42:33.634 --> 00:42:36.637
It's just that so far
all this has been about us...

524
00:42:36.804 --> 00:42:40.641
...how we can look good,
how we can get the glory.

525
00:42:42.560 --> 00:42:44.854
The more I read this book...

526
00:42:45.646 --> 00:42:47.899
...the more I realize
life's not about us.

527
00:42:48.775 --> 00:42:51.819
We're not here just to get glory,
make money and die.

528
00:42:51.986 --> 00:42:54.822
The Bible says that God
put us here for him.

529
00:42:54.989 --> 00:42:57.033
To honor him.

530
00:42:57.742 --> 00:43:00.161
Jesus said the most important
thing you could do with your life...

531
00:43:00.328 --> 00:43:03.498
...is to love God with everything
you are and love others as yourself.

532
00:43:04.165 --> 00:43:08.127
So if we win every game
and we miss that, we've done nothing.

533
00:43:08.753 --> 00:43:11.047
Football then means nothing.

534
00:43:12.048 --> 00:43:15.093
So I'm here to present you
a new team philosophy.

535
00:43:15.635 --> 00:43:19.347
I think that football is just one
of the tools we use to honor God.

536
00:43:19.514 --> 00:43:21.849
So you think God does care
about football?

537
00:43:22.016 --> 00:43:24.477
I think he cares
about your faith.

538
00:43:24.644 --> 00:43:26.896
He cares about
where your heart is.

539
00:43:27.063 --> 00:43:30.024
If you can live your faith out on the football
field, then, yes, God cares about football...

540
00:43:30.191 --> 00:43:31.818
...because he cares about you.

541
00:43:32.276 --> 00:43:35.363
He sent his son Jesus to die for us
so we could live for him.

542
00:43:35.530 --> 00:43:37.490
That's why we're here.

543
00:43:38.407 --> 00:43:41.202
But, see, it's not just
on the football field.

544
00:43:41.369 --> 00:43:43.955
We've gotta honor him
in our relationships...

545
00:43:44.122 --> 00:43:48.751
...in our respect for authority,
in the classroom...

546
00:43:49.335 --> 00:43:52.380
...and when you're at home alone
surfing the Internet.

547
00:43:57.093 --> 00:44:00.888
I want God to bless this team so much,
people talk about what he did.

548
00:44:01.055 --> 00:44:03.558
But it means we gotta give him
our best in every area.

549
00:44:03.724 --> 00:44:07.687
And if we win, we praise him.
And if we lose, we praise him.

550
00:44:07.854 --> 00:44:12.483
Either way, we honor him
with our actions and our attitudes.

551
00:44:13.276 --> 00:44:16.487
So I'm asking you,
what are you living for?

552
00:44:19.282 --> 00:44:22.243
I've resolved to give God
everything I've got...

553
00:44:22.410 --> 00:44:24.871
...then I'll leave the results
up to him.

554
00:44:26.747 --> 00:44:28.916
I wanna know if you'll join me.

555
00:44:30.251 --> 00:44:33.296
Your attitude's like the aroma
of your heart.

556
00:44:33.462 --> 00:44:36.549
If your attitude stinks,
it means your heart's not right.

557
00:44:37.592 --> 00:44:40.553
- He sure is preachy today.
- Mm-hm.

558
00:44:44.015 --> 00:44:45.433
What?

559
00:44:45.766 --> 00:44:47.768
How's your attitude, Brock?

560
00:44:48.269 --> 00:44:49.437
It's fine.

561
00:44:49.604 --> 00:44:51.272
Then you'll be okay
with the death crawl, right?

562
00:44:52.732 --> 00:44:55.776
All right, everybody on
the goal line. Get your partner. Let's go.

563
00:44:55.943 --> 00:44:57.278
All right, let's go.
Show me something.

564
00:44:57.445 --> 00:44:59.363
Ten yards. Move it, move it.
Let's go, let's go.

565
00:44:59.530 --> 00:45:03.618
Matt, let's go. Let's go, Jonathan.
Show me something. Ten yards.

566
00:45:03.784 --> 00:45:07.163
Show me some power. No knees.
Keep your knees off the ground.

567
00:45:07.330 --> 00:45:10.583
Show me something. Here we go.
Ten yards. Show me some muscle.

568
00:45:10.750 --> 00:45:14.086
Show me some power.
Give me some heart. Let's go.

569
00:45:14.253 --> 00:45:17.715
Very good, boys. Very good.
Let's run it back.

570
00:45:21.135 --> 00:45:23.804
Aw, man! Brock.

571
00:45:23.971 --> 00:45:25.473
Man, that's not
even funny, dude.

572
00:45:25.640 --> 00:45:26.807
Oh, yeah, it is.

573
00:45:27.266 --> 00:45:29.477
So, coach, how strong
is Westview this year?

574
00:45:29.644 --> 00:45:31.729
A lot stronger than we are.

575
00:45:32.438 --> 00:45:35.483
You already written Friday night
down as a loss, Brock?

576
00:45:35.691 --> 00:45:37.944
Well, not if I knew
we could beat them.

577
00:45:40.821 --> 00:45:42.615
Come here, Brock.
You too, Jeremy.

578
00:45:45.117 --> 00:45:47.203
What? Am I in trouble now?
Not yet.

579
00:45:47.370 --> 00:45:49.080
I wanna see you do
the death crawl again...

580
00:45:49.246 --> 00:45:50.498
...except I wanna see
your absolute best.

581
00:45:53.501 --> 00:45:55.628
What? You want me
to go the 30?

582
00:45:55.795 --> 00:45:58.965
- I think you can go to the 50.
- The 50?

583
00:45:59.131 --> 00:46:00.967
I can go to the 50
if nobody's on my back.

584
00:46:01.133 --> 00:46:03.094
I think you can do it
with Jeremy on your back.

585
00:46:03.260 --> 00:46:05.846
But even if you can't I want you
to promise me you're gonna do your best.

586
00:46:06.013 --> 00:46:07.264
All right.

587
00:46:07.431 --> 00:46:08.891
Your best.

588
00:46:09.058 --> 00:46:11.519
- Okay.
- You gonna give me your best?

589
00:46:11.686 --> 00:46:13.521
I'm gonna give you my best.

590
00:46:13.688 --> 00:46:15.106
All right, one more thing.

591
00:46:15.272 --> 00:46:17.692
- I want you to do it blindfolded.
- Why?

592
00:46:17.858 --> 00:46:21.112
I don't want you giving up at a
certain point when you can go further.

593
00:46:21.278 --> 00:46:23.698
Get down.
Jeremy, get on his back.

594
00:46:26.200 --> 00:46:28.119
Now, get a good
tight hold, Jeremy.

595
00:46:28.285 --> 00:46:30.997
All right.
Let's go, Brock.

596
00:46:31.247 --> 00:46:34.041
Keep your knees off the ground.
Just your hands and feet. There you go.

597
00:46:34.208 --> 00:46:35.501
A little bit left.
A little bit left.

598
00:46:35.668 --> 00:46:37.128
Come on, Brock. Come on.

599
00:46:37.294 --> 00:46:40.214
There you go.
Show me good effort.

600
00:46:41.465 --> 00:46:44.301
Thattaway, Brock.
You keep coming.

601
00:46:45.803 --> 00:46:48.180
- There you go.
- Come on, Brock.

602
00:46:48.347 --> 00:46:51.559
- Come on.
- It's a good start. Little bit left.

603
00:46:51.726 --> 00:46:53.436
Little bit left.

604
00:46:53.728 --> 00:46:55.604
There you go, Brock.

605
00:46:56.272 --> 00:46:58.065
Good strength.

606
00:47:00.484 --> 00:47:02.403
You gotta be kidding me.

607
00:47:03.738 --> 00:47:06.991
- That's it, Brock. That's it.
- Am I at the 20 yet?

608
00:47:07.158 --> 00:47:10.911
Forget the 20. You give me your best.
You keep going. That's it.

609
00:47:11.078 --> 00:47:13.539
Now don't stop, Brock.
You got more in you than that.

610
00:47:13.706 --> 00:47:15.332
I ain't done.
I'm just resting a second.

611
00:47:15.499 --> 00:47:17.209
You gotta keep moving.
Let's keep moving. Let's go.

612
00:47:17.376 --> 00:47:19.086
Don't quit till you got nothing left.

613
00:47:19.253 --> 00:47:22.631
There you go.
Keep moving. Keep moving.

614
00:47:23.049 --> 00:47:25.342
Keep moving, Brock.
That's it. You keep driving.

615
00:47:25.509 --> 00:47:28.471
Keep your knees off the ground.
Keep driving it. Your very best.

616
00:47:28.637 --> 00:47:30.890
Your very best. Your very best.

617
00:47:31.057 --> 00:47:34.185
Keep moving, Brock.
That's it. That's it. That's it.

618
00:47:34.351 --> 00:47:37.521
Keep going.
Don't quit on me. Keep going.

619
00:47:38.105 --> 00:47:40.941
Keep driving it. Keep your knees
off the ground. That's it.

620
00:47:41.108 --> 00:47:43.944
Your very best.
Don't quit on me. Your very best.

621
00:47:44.111 --> 00:47:47.573
Keep driving. Keep driving.
There you go. There you go.

622
00:47:47.740 --> 00:47:50.868
That's it. You keep driving. Keep your
knees off the ground. Keep driving it.

623
00:47:51.035 --> 00:47:53.746
Don't quit till you got nothing left.

624
00:47:53.913 --> 00:47:56.916
Keep moving, Brock.
That's it. That's it. That's it.

625
00:47:57.083 --> 00:48:00.628
Keep going. I want everything
you got. Come on, keep going.

626
00:48:01.879 --> 00:48:04.298
- It hurts.
- Don't quit on me. Your very best.

627
00:48:04.465 --> 00:48:08.594
Keep driving. Keep driving.
There you go. There you go.

628
00:48:08.761 --> 00:48:10.429
He's heavy.
I know he's heavy.

629
00:48:10.596 --> 00:48:11.680
I'm about out of strength.

630
00:48:11.847 --> 00:48:13.474
Then you negotiate with
your body to find more strength.

631
00:48:13.641 --> 00:48:15.976
But don't you give up on me, Brock.
You keep going, you hear me?

632
00:48:16.143 --> 00:48:18.229
You keep going.
You're doing good. You keep going.

633
00:48:18.395 --> 00:48:20.481
Do not quit on me.
You keep going.

634
00:48:20.648 --> 00:48:22.775
- It hurts.
- I know it hurts. You keep going.

635
00:48:22.942 --> 00:48:25.152
You keep going.
It's all heart from here.

636
00:48:25.319 --> 00:48:28.239
Thirty more steps.
You keep going, Brock. Come on.

637
00:48:28.405 --> 00:48:29.824
- Keep going.
- It burns.

638
00:48:29.990 --> 00:48:31.909
- Then let it burn.
- My arms are burning.

639
00:48:32.076 --> 00:48:34.495
It's all heart. You keep going,
Brock. Come on.

640
00:48:34.662 --> 00:48:38.833
Come on. Keep going.
You promised me your best. Your best.

641
00:48:38.999 --> 00:48:41.001
- Don't stop. Keep going.
- It's too hard.

642
00:48:41.168 --> 00:48:44.004
It's not too hard.
You keep going. Come on, Brock.

643
00:48:44.171 --> 00:48:47.174
Give me more.
Give me more. Keep going.

644
00:48:47.341 --> 00:48:49.343
Twenty more steps.
Twenty more.

645
00:48:49.510 --> 00:48:53.013
Keep going, Brock.
Give me your best. Don't quit.

646
00:48:53.180 --> 00:48:55.850
No. Keep going.
Keep going.

647
00:48:56.016 --> 00:48:59.562
Keep going.
Don't quit. Don't quit.

648
00:48:59.728 --> 00:49:02.565
Don't quit.
Brock Kelley, you don't quit.

649
00:49:02.731 --> 00:49:04.650
Keep going. Keep going.

650
00:49:04.817 --> 00:49:09.113
Go, Brock Kelley. You don't quit
on me. No, you keep going.

651
00:49:09.280 --> 00:49:11.448
You keep going.
Go, Brock.

652
00:49:11.615 --> 00:49:13.534
Ten more steps. Ten more.

653
00:49:13.701 --> 00:49:15.703
Ten more. Ten more.

654
00:49:15.870 --> 00:49:18.539
Keep going. Don't quit.
Give me your heart.

655
00:49:18.706 --> 00:49:21.625
- I can't do it.
- You can. You can.

656
00:49:21.792 --> 00:49:23.544
Five more. Five more.

657
00:49:23.711 --> 00:49:27.756
Come on, Brock. Come on.
Don't quit. Don't quit.

658
00:49:27.923 --> 00:49:31.802
Come on, Brock.
Two more. One more.

659
00:49:35.681 --> 00:49:37.474
That's gotta be fifty.

660
00:49:37.641 --> 00:49:40.561
That's gotta be fifty.
I don't have any more.

661
00:49:44.982 --> 00:49:48.319
Look up, Brock.
You're in the end zone.

662
00:49:54.909 --> 00:49:57.786
Brock, you are the most
influential player on this team.

663
00:49:57.953 --> 00:50:00.039
If you walk around defeated,
so will they.

664
00:50:01.415 --> 00:50:04.585
Don't tell me you can't
give me more than what I've been seeing.

665
00:50:04.752 --> 00:50:09.548
You just carried a 140-pound man
across this whole field on your arms.

666
00:50:12.384 --> 00:50:14.762
Brock, I need you.

667
00:50:15.137 --> 00:50:18.933
God's gifted you with the ability
of leadership. Don't waste it.

668
00:50:19.099 --> 00:50:20.726
Coach.

669
00:50:20.893 --> 00:50:22.937
Can I count on you?

670
00:50:25.773 --> 00:50:27.358
Yes.

671
00:50:29.068 --> 00:50:30.194
Coach.

672
00:50:31.278 --> 00:50:32.529
What is it, Jeremy?

673
00:50:33.113 --> 00:50:34.949
I weigh 160.

674
00:50:54.551 --> 00:50:57.805
All right. Who's next?

675
00:51:02.101 --> 00:51:05.896
Good practice, boys.
See you all tomorrow.

676
00:51:06.063 --> 00:51:09.817
Hey, man, for the first time in a while,
I actually feel good about Friday night.

677
00:51:09.984 --> 00:51:11.318
Yeah? Why?

678
00:51:11.485 --> 00:51:13.570
I'm just onboard
with what you're doing.

679
00:51:13.737 --> 00:51:16.532
If they get ahold of it,
it'll change their lives.

680
00:51:16.699 --> 00:51:18.826
You count me in.

681
00:51:21.996 --> 00:51:24.873
Grant, me too.

682
00:51:25.291 --> 00:51:26.417
Yeah?

683
00:51:26.583 --> 00:51:27.918
Yeah.

684
00:51:28.085 --> 00:51:30.504
I feel like I owe you
an apology.

685
00:51:30.754 --> 00:51:33.841
I just want you to know
that I'm with you.

686
00:51:35.134 --> 00:51:36.385
Thank you.

687
00:51:36.552 --> 00:51:38.429
See you tomorrow.

688
00:51:54.778 --> 00:51:57.614
- You need a ride, Matt?
- No, my dad's coming.

689
00:51:57.781 --> 00:51:59.950
Or at least, he'd better be.

690
00:52:01.660 --> 00:52:03.704
Can I shoot straight
with you for a minute?

691
00:52:03.871 --> 00:52:05.414
Sure.

692
00:52:05.581 --> 00:52:07.541
I feel like you owe
your dad more respect.

693
00:52:07.708 --> 00:52:09.501
- Why?
- Because he's your father.

694
00:52:09.668 --> 00:52:12.296
- You don't know him like I know him.
- I don't have to know him.

695
00:52:12.463 --> 00:52:14.882
You need to respect him
because it's the right thing to do.

696
00:52:15.049 --> 00:52:18.010
You know, coach,
my dad doesn't even like you.

697
00:52:18.427 --> 00:52:21.221
He thinks the school needs
to find somebody else.

698
00:52:21.388 --> 00:52:24.391
That's beside the point.
Scripture says to honor your parents.

699
00:52:24.558 --> 00:52:27.686
- And all you do is complain.
- All he does is boss me around.

700
00:52:27.853 --> 00:52:29.938
He doesn't even try
to understand me.

701
00:52:30.105 --> 00:52:32.441
Matt, you can't judge
your father by his actions...

702
00:52:32.608 --> 00:52:34.401
...and then judge yourself
by your intentions.

703
00:52:34.568 --> 00:52:37.196
It doesn't work that way.
You're not responsible for him.

704
00:52:37.363 --> 00:52:40.699
You're responsible for you. You honor
God by honoring your authority.

705
00:52:41.492 --> 00:52:45.162
You really believe in all that
honoring God and follow Jesus stuff?

706
00:52:46.121 --> 00:52:47.164
Yes, I do.

707
00:52:48.540 --> 00:52:51.585
Well, I ain't trying
to be disrespectful...

708
00:52:51.752 --> 00:52:53.754
...but not everybody
believes in that.

709
00:52:53.921 --> 00:52:55.756
Religion works
for some people...

710
00:52:55.923 --> 00:52:58.675
...but I'm just here because
I got kicked out of Westview.

711
00:52:58.842 --> 00:53:01.887
Matt, nobody's forcing anything
on you. Following Jesus Christ...

712
00:53:02.054 --> 00:53:04.723
...is a decision you're gonna
have to make for yourself.

713
00:53:04.890 --> 00:53:06.475
You may not wanna accept him.

714
00:53:06.642 --> 00:53:10.187
Because he'll change your life.
You'll never be the same.

715
00:53:11.146 --> 00:53:14.024
I do hope one day you realize
how much he loves you.

716
00:53:15.109 --> 00:53:16.777
I'll see you tomorrow.

717
00:53:26.912 --> 00:53:28.789
Okay. I'll get him.
Just give me the bag.

718
00:53:28.956 --> 00:53:30.666
Just bring that trash bag
over here. Set it down.

719
00:53:30.833 --> 00:53:31.959
Ooh, don't you
let that touch me.

720
00:53:32.126 --> 00:53:34.795
I'm not gonna let him touch you, Brooke.
I'm gonna get him out of here.

721
00:53:34.962 --> 00:53:36.171
Oh, man, he stinks.

722
00:53:36.338 --> 00:53:38.882
Ooh, I can't believe
that was in my house.

723
00:53:39.049 --> 00:53:40.968
- Just make sure it's still dead.
- It's dead.

724
00:53:41.135 --> 00:53:43.637
He's probably been dead
for weeks. Oh, there you go.

725
00:53:43.804 --> 00:53:46.014
You just get it out of here.
Out. Out.

726
00:53:46.181 --> 00:53:47.724
Stop being af... Come here.

727
00:53:47.891 --> 00:53:49.017
- Just look at it.
- Mm-mm. No.

728
00:53:49.184 --> 00:53:50.394
It looks like a big hamster.

729
00:53:50.561 --> 00:53:52.187
- Oh, uh-uh.
- Just... Come here, come here.

730
00:53:52.354 --> 00:53:54.648
Don't be afraid.
Just face your fear. Look.

731
00:53:54.815 --> 00:53:56.316
He's got a cute little tail there.

732
00:53:56.483 --> 00:54:01.321
He's just got a big stink.
Look. See his cute little eyes there?

733
00:54:01.488 --> 00:54:04.283
See his teeth? Look at his teeth.
Almost looks like he's mad.

734
00:54:04.450 --> 00:54:06.243
- Aagghh!
- Oh! Oh!

735
00:54:06.410 --> 00:54:10.205
You're terrible. I can't believe
you did that to me, Grant Taylor.

736
00:54:10.372 --> 00:54:11.999
You are so bad.

737
00:54:12.166 --> 00:54:13.876
Whoo!

738
00:54:16.086 --> 00:54:19.006
David, right down
the middle. You got this.

739
00:54:21.008 --> 00:54:22.926
All right, set it up. Run it again.

740
00:54:23.093 --> 00:54:26.680
Sorry, coach.
David, listen, son.

741
00:54:26.847 --> 00:54:29.725
You act like you gonna miss
before you even kick the ball.

742
00:54:29.892 --> 00:54:32.769
See, we're gonna have to change
your whole kicking philosophy.

743
00:54:32.936 --> 00:54:36.356
Now, see, you're kicking
wide left or wide right.

744
00:54:36.523 --> 00:54:38.400
But that ain't what's gonna
get you home.

745
00:54:38.567 --> 00:54:41.195
The ball has got to go
through the middle.

746
00:54:41.361 --> 00:54:43.822
- I know, coach.
- No. No, you don't.

747
00:54:43.989 --> 00:54:46.033
Now, what does Scripture
say about this?

748
00:54:46.742 --> 00:54:47.784
Um...

749
00:54:47.951 --> 00:54:49.912
Scripture says: Wide is the gate...

750
00:54:50.078 --> 00:54:52.498
...and broad is the way
that leads to destruction...

751
00:54:52.664 --> 00:54:54.791
...and many there be that find it.

752
00:54:54.958 --> 00:54:58.212
Now, to us, that's wide left
and wide right.

753
00:54:58.378 --> 00:54:59.421
Well!

754
00:54:59.588 --> 00:55:03.550
But narrow is the gate and straight
is the way that leads to life...

755
00:55:03.717 --> 00:55:06.553
- ...and few there be that find it.
- Well!

756
00:55:06.720 --> 00:55:09.848
Anybody can kick it
wide left or wide right.

757
00:55:10.015 --> 00:55:13.560
My mama can kick it
wide left and wide right.

758
00:55:13.727 --> 00:55:15.229
But that ain't what's
gonna get you home.

759
00:55:15.395 --> 00:55:16.563
Come on!

760
00:55:16.730 --> 00:55:19.900
It don't have to look pretty.
It don't have to look smooth.

761
00:55:20.067 --> 00:55:22.027
It can look like a dying duck.

762
00:55:22.194 --> 00:55:24.905
But the ball has to go
through the middle.

763
00:55:25.072 --> 00:55:26.573
Oh, my word!

764
00:55:26.740 --> 00:55:29.201
Now, David, you gonna have
to choose the narrow way.

765
00:55:29.826 --> 00:55:32.287
That's the only path where
you will get your reward.

766
00:55:32.454 --> 00:55:34.581
Now send this ball
through these pearly posts.

767
00:55:34.748 --> 00:55:36.583
Set it up one more
time for me, Jonathan.

768
00:55:36.750 --> 00:55:39.002
David, I've never heard it
that way before...

769
00:55:39.169 --> 00:55:41.713
...but there's a lot of truth
to what he's saying.

770
00:55:41.880 --> 00:55:43.507
Let's see you kick it.

771
00:55:53.475 --> 00:55:55.978
Yeah, that's what
I'm talking about.

772
00:56:00.732 --> 00:56:04.194
Grant, are you not aware of what's
going on outside on the field?

773
00:56:04.361 --> 00:56:05.404
What?

774
00:56:05.571 --> 00:56:07.781
You might wanna
come check this out.

775
00:56:10.492 --> 00:56:13.203
Mitch decided to bring
his Bible class outside today.

776
00:56:13.370 --> 00:56:16.665
After he started teaching,
Matt Prater accepted Christ as his Lord.

777
00:56:16.832 --> 00:56:19.960
It was awesome. He started
confessing stuff from his life...

778
00:56:20.127 --> 00:56:22.421
...he started asking his friends
for forgiveness.

779
00:56:22.588 --> 00:56:25.674
Next thing we know, Bob Duke
stands up and does the same thing.

780
00:56:25.841 --> 00:56:29.094
Kids start breaking up into groups,
they begin to pray for each other.

781
00:56:29.261 --> 00:56:31.638
They begin to ask forgiveness
for sins that they've committed.

782
00:56:31.805 --> 00:56:33.307
This has been going on
for three hours.

783
00:56:33.473 --> 00:56:35.851
How did you not know
what was going on?

784
00:57:08.342 --> 00:57:12.179
Bless them in a special way.
Lord, I ask you to lift them up to you.

785
00:57:16.558 --> 00:57:20.354
I ask you to bring up a generation
that has a heart for you, Lord.

786
00:57:23.732 --> 00:57:25.233
Coach.

787
00:57:30.155 --> 00:57:33.700
- I'm proud of you, Matt.
- I need to talk with my dad.

788
00:57:33.867 --> 00:57:36.036
I'd like to go see him.

789
00:57:37.371 --> 00:57:39.414
I'll take you right now.

790
00:57:41.375 --> 00:57:44.211
So, what we've done here
is we've gained these four lots...

791
00:57:44.378 --> 00:57:46.421
...by moving the retention pond
down here.

792
00:57:46.588 --> 00:57:48.382
We could try and do that
through here if you want.

793
00:57:48.548 --> 00:57:50.300
No. I like this.
That's perfect.

794
00:57:51.677 --> 00:57:53.929
<i>Mr. Prater,
there's someone here to see you.</i>

795
00:57:54.096 --> 00:57:55.389
Sarah, I'm in a meeting.

796
00:57:55.555 --> 00:57:57.557
<i>Um, it's your son.</i>

797
00:57:58.642 --> 00:58:01.311
Would you like me to step out?
No, it's okay.

798
00:58:01.478 --> 00:58:03.522
Sarah, send him in.

799
00:58:09.152 --> 00:58:10.320
Matt, you okay?

800
00:58:10.988 --> 00:58:13.407
I'm sorry, Dad. I didn't know
you were in a meeting.

801
00:58:13.573 --> 00:58:14.658
What is it, son?

802
00:58:16.284 --> 00:58:20.747
Uh, Dad, I just wanted
to say that I'm sorry.

803
00:58:21.707 --> 00:58:23.458
I'm sorry for the way
I've been acting.

804
00:58:25.502 --> 00:58:27.838
I got right with God today...

805
00:58:28.005 --> 00:58:31.717
...and I just needed to say
that from now on...

806
00:58:31.883 --> 00:58:34.219
...I'll respect your authority.

807
00:58:34.386 --> 00:58:36.805
Whatever you say goes.

808
00:58:38.265 --> 00:58:39.850
That's it.

809
00:58:43.478 --> 00:58:45.272
You know, I could
come back tomorrow...

810
00:58:45.439 --> 00:58:47.065
...if that would be better for you.

811
00:58:47.232 --> 00:58:50.027
No. It's okay.

812
00:58:50.193 --> 00:58:52.362
I'm sorry. I, uh...

813
00:59:06.293 --> 00:59:08.211
For what it's worth...

814
00:59:08.378 --> 00:59:12.299
...I'd give my right arm
to hear my son say that to me.

815
00:59:18.597 --> 00:59:20.932
I feel like I'm standing
before a new team tonight.

816
00:59:22.601 --> 00:59:24.311
It's a new day and a new game.

817
00:59:25.937 --> 00:59:27.439
What you've experienced
in your hearts this week...

818
00:59:27.606 --> 00:59:29.983
...is about to be released on the field.

819
00:59:30.150 --> 00:59:32.402
Stay humble but confident.

820
00:59:33.820 --> 00:59:35.864
Why don't you
take this one, Brock?

821
00:59:39.910 --> 00:59:42.788
Lord, we know
our lives are not about football...

822
00:59:42.954 --> 00:59:45.499
...but we do thank you
for allowing us to play tonight.

823
00:59:45.999 --> 00:59:47.793
Lord, we're gonna
give you our best.

824
00:59:47.959 --> 00:59:50.921
If we win, we'll praise you,
and if we lose, we'll praise you.

825
00:59:51.588 --> 00:59:54.341
We'll give you all the honor and the glory
for this night, Lord. Keep us safe.

826
00:59:54.508 --> 00:59:57.594
- In Jesus' name we pray. Amen.
- Amen.

827
00:59:57.761 --> 01:00:00.180
All right, guys. Look at me.

828
01:00:00.597 --> 01:00:02.974
Play hard, have fun.

829
01:00:09.523 --> 01:00:10.899
Hit.

830
01:00:25.705 --> 01:00:27.040
Yeah!

831
01:00:29.251 --> 01:00:31.086
Yeah!

832
01:01:09.082 --> 01:01:11.585
In the Old Testament,
Nehemiah had the task of building...

833
01:01:11.751 --> 01:01:13.879
...a stone wall around his city
for protection.

834
01:01:14.045 --> 01:01:16.923
But he didn't have enough people
or resources or time.

835
01:01:17.090 --> 01:01:18.842
But because each person worked on...

836
01:01:19.009 --> 01:01:20.302
...the stone wall
that was in front of their house...

837
01:01:20.468 --> 01:01:23.471
...they got it done in record time.
That's what you're gonna do.

838
01:01:23.638 --> 01:01:27.726
On defense you have to resolve
nothing gets by you as an individual...

839
01:01:27.893 --> 01:01:30.020
...nothing gets by us as a team.

840
01:01:30.187 --> 01:01:32.397
I need you to build me
a stone wall.

841
01:01:41.948 --> 01:01:43.867
Get on that, D.

842
01:01:52.292 --> 01:01:53.793
Yeah.

843
01:02:20.237 --> 01:02:22.113
Let's go. Let's go.

844
01:02:22.280 --> 01:02:25.575
Roll through there like you're
soul-struck. Come on, now.

845
01:02:25.742 --> 01:02:27.202
Come on, Brocky-Brock.
Hit somebody, son.

846
01:02:27.369 --> 01:02:29.621
I wanna see some hitting.
I wanna see some hitting.

847
01:02:29.788 --> 01:02:32.040
Dig those feet. Come on,
you ain't on my team yet.

848
01:02:32.207 --> 01:02:34.542
You're not on my defense.
You gotta dig those feet.

849
01:02:34.709 --> 01:02:37.170
All right, Prater. Get in there, boy.
Let's go. Hit him.

850
01:02:37.337 --> 01:02:39.339
Hit him, son. You gotta hit him
a little harder than that.

851
01:02:39.506 --> 01:02:42.342
This ain't ballet practice.
This is football practice.

852
01:03:12.372 --> 01:03:14.207
David.

853
01:03:14.457 --> 01:03:15.959
David.

854
01:03:32.851 --> 01:03:34.477
Double-sweep pitch left.

855
01:03:34.644 --> 01:03:37.731
Pro 45 flex. Man, even
a 26 Powerhouse.

856
01:03:37.897 --> 01:03:39.816
Man, these are some good plays.
When we gonna run these plays?

857
01:03:39.983 --> 01:03:41.026
We're gonna run them.

858
01:03:41.192 --> 01:03:43.987
Man, we got all type of potential
on this sheet. When?

859
01:03:44.154 --> 01:03:46.114
- We're gonna run them, I promise.
- Yeah, see?

860
01:03:46.281 --> 01:03:48.616
You always tell me you're gonna
run them. See, all my plays...

861
01:03:48.783 --> 01:03:50.994
- You don't wanna run my plays.
- Hey!

862
01:03:51.161 --> 01:03:52.245
It's all right.

863
01:03:52.412 --> 01:03:53.747
Where's my car?

864
01:03:53.913 --> 01:03:57.250
- Where'd you park it?
- Right here.

865
01:03:57.417 --> 01:04:01.046
You sure? Because there
ain't no way it got stolen.

866
01:04:01.212 --> 01:04:03.340
Man, you couldn't pay
nobody to steal your car.

867
01:04:03.506 --> 01:04:06.760
- Did the boys do something with it?
- Man, I don't know.

868
01:04:07.177 --> 01:04:10.096
Hey, man, there's a note
on this truck for you.

869
01:04:11.097 --> 01:04:14.059
- What does it say?
- Let's see.

870
01:04:14.309 --> 01:04:17.479
It says, "Grant Taylor,
the impact you made on our school...

871
01:04:17.645 --> 01:04:19.773
...means more to us
than you'll ever know.

872
01:04:19.939 --> 01:04:22.359
The Lord has used you
to meet a need in our lives...

873
01:04:22.525 --> 01:04:24.486
...and now we want
to meet a need in yours.

874
01:04:24.652 --> 01:04:28.114
You'll find the title of this
new truck in your name.

875
01:04:28.281 --> 01:04:31.910
Please accept it as our way
of saying thank you."

876
01:04:33.286 --> 01:04:34.788
Uh-uh.

877
01:04:34.954 --> 01:04:37.624
Somebody done gave you a truck?

878
01:04:44.172 --> 01:04:46.883
Man, this title
got your name on it.

879
01:04:55.600 --> 01:04:57.310
You got to be kidding me.

880
01:05:03.274 --> 01:05:07.695
Grant Taylor, somebody
done gave you a new truck.

881
01:05:08.863 --> 01:05:10.865
This is my truck?

882
01:05:27.507 --> 01:05:30.009
Is this just because
you head coach?

883
01:05:30.176 --> 01:05:32.387
Because I'm assistant coach.

884
01:05:33.012 --> 01:05:36.307
You'd think I'd get a moped
out of this or something.

885
01:05:44.607 --> 01:05:47.527
Oh, Lord, you've given me a truck.

886
01:05:48.236 --> 01:05:52.740
Well, it's your truck. Drive it.

887
01:05:55.785 --> 01:05:58.037
Not a word to anyone.

888
01:05:58.204 --> 01:05:59.914
Yes, sir.

889
01:06:07.881 --> 01:06:11.593
That's right.
No more jumper cables.

890
01:06:14.429 --> 01:06:15.805
Break.

891
01:06:17.390 --> 01:06:19.559
Brock. Brock.

892
01:06:19.726 --> 01:06:23.646
- You watch him. You watch him.
- Sure.

893
01:06:23.813 --> 01:06:25.231
Hut, hut.

894
01:06:38.244 --> 01:06:40.413
- Go.
- Go. Go.

895
01:07:11.778 --> 01:07:17.242
That's right. That's it, baby.
You got it, Brock.

896
01:07:18.451 --> 01:07:19.786
That's right.

897
01:07:39.639 --> 01:07:41.808
- Yes, sir? Can I help you?
- Uh, please.

898
01:07:41.975 --> 01:07:45.937
I'd like to buy a nice bouquet
of wildflowers for my wife.

899
01:07:46.104 --> 01:07:48.481
I see.
That's awfully sweet of you.

900
01:07:48.648 --> 01:07:52.235
Oh, yes. I've got a special evening
in mind for her tonight.

901
01:07:52.402 --> 01:07:55.738
Well, in that case, you need a card
to go with those flowers, don't you?

902
01:07:55.905 --> 01:07:57.615
Oh, no. I've already got
the perfect one.

903
01:07:57.782 --> 01:08:00.243
I'm gonna give it to her
at her favorite restaurant this evening.

904
01:08:00.410 --> 01:08:02.996
Oh, really?
I'm sure she'll be happy.

905
01:08:03.162 --> 01:08:07.458
Oh, she will. So I need
your nicest, largest flowers...

906
01:08:07.625 --> 01:08:10.086
- ...and money's no object.
- Oh?

907
01:08:10.253 --> 01:08:14.173
- You see, I got a raise today.
- You did?

908
01:08:14.340 --> 01:08:17.760
- Six thousand dollars.
- Are you serious?

909
01:08:17.927 --> 01:08:19.679
You know, that's exactly the way
my wife's gonna respond.

910
01:08:19.846 --> 01:08:21.973
Oh, Grant!

911
01:08:22.682 --> 01:08:24.100
Oh, Grant!

912
01:08:24.267 --> 01:08:25.685
That's awesome.

913
01:08:25.852 --> 01:08:28.187
You know, you sure got
friendly service here.

914
01:08:35.028 --> 01:08:36.863
<i>Hello again, everybody.
This is Lane Lavarre...</i>

915
01:08:37.030 --> 01:08:38.948
...along with my broadcast
partner, Dale Hansen...

916
01:08:39.115 --> 01:08:41.784
...coming to you tonight from
Princeton Heights Academy...

917
01:08:41.951 --> 01:08:45.163
...the site of tonight's opening round
of the GISA football playoffs.

918
01:08:45.330 --> 01:08:47.040
For the first time
in a decade...

919
01:08:47.206 --> 01:08:49.792
<i>...the Shiloh Eagles find themselves
in postseason play.</i>

920
01:08:49.959 --> 01:08:52.378
<i>And Coach Grant Taylor's
gonna have his hands full tonight...</i>

921
01:08:52.545 --> 01:08:54.172
...as he takes on the
number-one-seeded Panthers...

922
01:08:54.339 --> 01:08:55.840
...who haven't lost
a game all season.

923
01:08:56.466 --> 01:09:00.303
All right, huddle up. Stay sharp,
stay focused, play hard and honor God.

924
01:09:00.470 --> 01:09:02.889
- Eagles on three. One, two, three.
- Eagles.

925
01:09:05.058 --> 01:09:06.976
Sweep.

926
01:09:39.926 --> 01:09:42.136
<i>So after an impressive
seven- and-three record...</i>

927
01:09:42.303 --> 01:09:46.015
<i>...the Shiloh Eagles fall short tonight
in the first round of the GISA playoffs.</i>

928
01:09:46.182 --> 01:09:47.725
Twenty-eight to 10
is the final score.

929
01:09:47.892 --> 01:09:50.853
The Princeton Heights Panthers
take it to the Shiloh Eagles.

930
01:09:52.355 --> 01:09:54.774
I knew we were gonna
get killed tonight.

931
01:10:08.037 --> 01:10:11.582
Your effort was good tonight.
You've got nothing to be ashamed of.

932
01:10:16.129 --> 01:10:17.964
You played hard.

933
01:10:18.339 --> 01:10:21.050
The Shilohs had the best season
they've had in a long time.

934
01:10:21.217 --> 01:10:23.469
God's been good to us this year.

935
01:10:30.268 --> 01:10:32.395
Guys, coach is right.

936
01:10:32.562 --> 01:10:34.814
We're gonna praise God
when we win...

937
01:10:34.981 --> 01:10:36.482
...we're gonna praise him
when we lose.

938
01:10:39.652 --> 01:10:41.237
Let's take a knee.

939
01:10:57.128 --> 01:10:59.756
- Hey.
- Hey.

940
01:11:03.885 --> 01:11:07.472
I wish by some miracle
we could have won tonight.

941
01:11:08.347 --> 01:11:11.559
They worked too hard to walk away
with their heads down.

942
01:11:14.187 --> 01:11:18.441
You know, I was hoping God would
give us just one win in the playoffs.

943
01:11:21.694 --> 01:11:23.696
They deserved it.

944
01:11:31.579 --> 01:11:33.664
You know, if you'd told me
two months ago...

945
01:11:33.831 --> 01:11:36.584
...that we'd be playing
Princeton Heights in the playoffs...

946
01:11:36.751 --> 01:11:38.878
- ...I would not have believed you.
- Yeah.

947
01:11:39.045 --> 01:11:41.297
If you'd told me our school
was having a revival this year...

948
01:11:41.464 --> 01:11:44.133
...I wouldn't have believed you either.
But this ain't been a bad year.

949
01:11:44.300 --> 01:11:45.343
Got all the jerseys?

950
01:11:45.510 --> 01:11:48.221
All 32 of them. But I ain't
ready to put them up, though.

951
01:11:48.387 --> 01:11:50.097
I'm ready to go another round.

952
01:11:50.264 --> 01:11:53.226
You and me both.
Part of me wanted to get to state.

953
01:11:53.392 --> 01:11:55.978
To state?
Grant, are you serious?

954
01:11:56.145 --> 01:11:57.647
Why not? As hard as they worked?

955
01:11:57.814 --> 01:12:00.733
Well, working hard is one thing,
but to take this team to state?

956
01:12:00.900 --> 01:12:04.153
- That'd take an act of God.
- Has he not been acting already?

957
01:12:04.320 --> 01:12:05.780
Well, yeah, he has, but do you know...

958
01:12:05.947 --> 01:12:08.074
...who's gonna be waiting
for whoever gets to state?

959
01:12:08.241 --> 01:12:10.910
- The Richland Giants.
- That's right, the Richland Giants.

960
01:12:11.077 --> 01:12:13.788
And Bobby Lee Duke will be
there with his 85 players...

961
01:12:13.955 --> 01:12:18.167
...ready to spank whoever made it
to the state playoffs to kingdom come.

962
01:12:18.334 --> 01:12:20.920
- I'm not afraid.
- I know you're not afraid.

963
01:12:21.087 --> 01:12:22.255
Because you ain't going.

964
01:12:22.421 --> 01:12:25.216
Oh, by the way, man,
some man called looking for you today.

965
01:12:25.383 --> 01:12:26.592
Who?

966
01:12:26.759 --> 01:12:28.845
Stan Shultz.

967
01:12:29.011 --> 01:12:30.596
- Stan Shultz?
- Yeah.

968
01:12:31.597 --> 01:12:34.350
Stan Shultz.
Isn't that the cartoonist?

969
01:12:34.517 --> 01:12:36.269
That's Charles Schulz.

970
01:12:36.435 --> 01:12:39.522
No, I thought Charles Schulz was
that man that flew across the ocean...

971
01:12:39.689 --> 01:12:41.148
...in the<i> Spirit of St. Andrew.</i>

972
01:12:41.315 --> 01:12:44.235
That's Charles Lindbergh,
and it was the<i> Spirit of St. Louis.</i>

973
01:12:44.402 --> 01:12:47.613
- No, Lindbergh is a cheese.
- Limburger's the cheese.

974
01:12:47.780 --> 01:12:48.906
Lindbergh's the man.

975
01:12:49.282 --> 01:12:53.411
No, Lindbergh was that blimp that
blew up and killed all them people.

976
01:12:54.745 --> 01:12:57.123
That's the<i> Hindenburg.</i>

977
01:13:00.042 --> 01:13:02.962
No, Hindenburg is where
you go skiing in Tennessee.

978
01:13:03.129 --> 01:13:04.630
That's Gatlinburg.

979
01:13:04.797 --> 01:13:05.798
Gatlinburg?

980
01:13:05.965 --> 01:13:09.302
You mean like the country-music
group, the Gatlinburg Brothers?

981
01:13:11.220 --> 01:13:13.389
You guys are crazy.

982
01:13:14.932 --> 01:13:16.684
Grant Taylor.

983
01:13:17.518 --> 01:13:21.063
Well, Mr. Shultz, I was told
you were looking for me.

984
01:13:21.439 --> 01:13:23.024
Yes.

985
01:13:23.190 --> 01:13:25.735
Am I sitting down?
Why do you ask?

986
01:13:28.696 --> 01:13:30.823
Hey, coach,
what's going on here?

987
01:13:30.990 --> 01:13:32.825
Coach is on his way
to let us all know.

988
01:13:32.992 --> 01:13:34.660
All right.

989
01:13:37.163 --> 01:13:39.165
All right, everybody.
Bring it in.

990
01:13:44.003 --> 01:13:45.963
I want you to know
I serve a big God...

991
01:13:46.130 --> 01:13:48.132
...and he can do whatever
he wants to do.

992
01:13:48.299 --> 01:13:50.843
He can open what he wants to open
and shut what he wants to shut.

993
01:13:51.010 --> 01:13:53.012
And a team that plays
for his honor and glory...

994
01:13:53.179 --> 01:13:55.306
...will have his blessings
following that team.

995
01:13:55.473 --> 01:13:58.601
Unlike those who try to cheat their way
to the top, like Princeton Heights did...

996
01:13:58.768 --> 01:14:02.313
...in last Friday's game when they played
two ineligible 19-year-olds.

997
01:14:02.480 --> 01:14:05.483
They have been disqualified
and we're advancing to the next round.

998
01:14:05.650 --> 01:14:07.860
Get your pads on
for practice, boys.

999
01:14:08.027 --> 01:14:09.445
We're going to war
with Tucker Friday night.

1000
01:14:19.372 --> 01:14:22.375
<i>Welcome, ladies and
gentlemen, to the GISA quarterfinals.</i>

1001
01:14:22.541 --> 01:14:26.045
Who in the world would have thought that
we'd be seeing the Shiloh Eagles tonight...

1002
01:14:26.212 --> 01:14:28.130
...in a contest against
the Tucker Tigers?

1003
01:14:28.297 --> 01:14:30.049
Well, with Princeton Heights
being disqualified...

1004
01:14:30.216 --> 01:14:32.802
...you could call this an early
Christmas present for Shiloh.

1005
01:14:32.969 --> 01:14:35.763
Offense, put it in the end zone.
Defense, build me a stone wall.

1006
01:14:35.930 --> 01:14:38.474
- Eagles on three. One, two, three.
- Eagles.

1007
01:14:42.728 --> 01:14:45.773
Blue, 18. Blue, 18.

1008
01:14:45.940 --> 01:14:48.859
Set. Hit. Hit.

1009
01:15:11.090 --> 01:15:12.591
David.

1010
01:15:13.676 --> 01:15:16.595
This is your field goal.
It belongs to you. Put it through.

1011
01:15:16.762 --> 01:15:18.848
We're putting David in.

1012
01:15:23.561 --> 01:15:24.687
David.

1013
01:15:27.106 --> 01:15:28.524
Hit.

1014
01:15:31.944 --> 01:15:33.487
Yeah!

1015
01:15:33.654 --> 01:15:36.782
There you go. There you go.

1016
01:15:36.991 --> 01:15:39.535
With the clock running down, the
Tucker Tigers are nursing their wounds...

1017
01:15:39.702 --> 01:15:41.537
...as they face
the end of their season.

1018
01:15:41.704 --> 01:15:44.623
The Eagles, however,
have a little farther to fly.

1019
01:15:45.750 --> 01:15:48.002
All right, what kind of sick
are we talking about?

1020
01:15:48.169 --> 01:15:51.255
I don't know. I've just felt really
nauseous the last two mornings.

1021
01:15:51.422 --> 01:15:52.631
And then I feel fine again.

1022
01:15:52.965 --> 01:15:55.134
And you haven't eaten
anything weird lately?

1023
01:15:55.301 --> 01:15:57.428
Not unless fruit
and cereal's weird.

1024
01:15:58.679 --> 01:16:02.349
Brooke, my gut says make
an appointment with the doctor.

1025
01:16:02.683 --> 01:16:06.896
I've been there three times this year.
It's getting embarrassing.

1026
01:16:07.063 --> 01:16:10.274
I'm just telling you what I would do.
You can even use my car.

1027
01:16:15.112 --> 01:16:16.739
<i>With five seconds left in the game...</i>

1028
01:16:16.906 --> 01:16:18.699
<i>...the score still stands
in Oakhaven's favor...</i>

1029
01:16:18.866 --> 01:16:20.868
<i>...17-14 over the Eagles.</i>

1030
01:16:21.035 --> 01:16:23.162
<i>Grant Taylor calls the play in
to Zach Avery...</i>

1031
01:16:23.329 --> 01:16:26.665
<i>...who pulls the huddle together
for their last shot at going to state.</i>

1032
01:16:26.832 --> 01:16:30.294
<i>It's third down and goal for the Eagles
and the crowd is going crazy.</i>

1033
01:16:30.461 --> 01:16:33.798
<i>They line up in an I formation.
This is do or die for the Eagles.</i>

1034
01:16:33.964 --> 01:16:36.217
<i>Zach takes the snap and
will give it to Jacob Hall for...</i>

1035
01:16:36.383 --> 01:16:37.676
<i>No, wait a minute, it's a fake.</i>

1036
01:16:37.843 --> 01:16:41.180
<i>He's got Nathan Markle open in the
corner. The pass is up. He's got it.</i>

1037
01:16:41.347 --> 01:16:44.475
<i>Touchdown Eagles!
Touchdown Eagles!</i>

1038
01:16:44.642 --> 01:16:46.894
<i>Zach Avery completely
faked out the defense...</i>

1039
01:16:47.061 --> 01:16:49.897
<i>...and made a perfect pass
to win the game 20 to 17.</i>

1040
01:16:50.064 --> 01:16:51.440
<i>Can you believe this?</i>

1041
01:16:51.607 --> 01:16:55.528
<i>The Shiloh Eagles are actually
headed to the state championship.</i>

1042
01:16:55.694 --> 01:17:00.491
<i>A team with only 32 players
has made it to the big dance. Oh, my.</i>

1043
01:17:00.658 --> 01:17:03.536
{\an8}<i>On the eve of the GISA high-school</i>
<i>football state championship...</i>

1044
01:17:03.702 --> 01:17:06.580
{\an8}<i>...the Richland Giants prepare</i>
<i>to defend their three-year reign...</i>

1045
01:17:06.747 --> 01:17:08.040
{\an8}<i>...as lords of the gridiron.</i>

1046
01:17:08.207 --> 01:17:10.417
{\an8}<i>It's no surprise they've</i>
<i>returned for this game.</i>

1047
01:17:10.584 --> 01:17:12.628
{\an8}<i>What is surprising</i>
<i>is who they're playing.</i>

1048
01:17:12.795 --> 01:17:17.091
{\an8}<i>The Shiloh Eagles, who started the</i>
<i>season 0-3, have come out of nowhere...</i>

1049
01:17:17.258 --> 01:17:19.677
{\an8}<i>...and through an almost bizarre</i>
<i>set of circumstances...</i>

1050
01:17:19.844 --> 01:17:22.555
{\an8}<i>...now face a team</i>
<i>almost three times their size.</i>

1051
01:17:32.148 --> 01:17:34.400
Sleep at all last night?

1052
01:17:34.900 --> 01:17:36.694
Mm-mm.

1053
01:17:36.902 --> 01:17:38.237
Are you nervous?

1054
01:17:39.071 --> 01:17:40.781
It's a weird emotion.

1055
01:17:40.948 --> 01:17:43.742
Part of me thinks we're
gonna get crushed tonight...

1056
01:17:44.577 --> 01:17:47.246
...part of me thinks God may
do something awesome.

1057
01:17:47.830 --> 01:17:50.541
Sounds like your fear's
about to clobber your faith.

1058
01:17:51.750 --> 01:17:54.587
Hmm. Something like that.

1059
01:17:55.004 --> 01:17:57.173
When are you going out there?

1060
01:17:57.715 --> 01:17:59.925
I might leave early,
if that's all right.

1061
01:18:00.092 --> 01:18:02.761
Yeah, just don't worry about me.
I'll just meet you at the game.

1062
01:18:02.928 --> 01:18:04.430
Okay.

1063
01:18:06.849 --> 01:18:09.560
Either way, you're still playing
for a state championship.

1064
01:18:13.105 --> 01:18:14.523
Hmm.

1065
01:18:19.904 --> 01:18:22.823
Juice. There's some juice.

1066
01:18:24.158 --> 01:18:25.618
Do you see that?

1067
01:18:28.120 --> 01:18:29.580
This is?

1068
01:18:30.831 --> 01:18:33.042
- Apple.
- Apple. Good.

1069
01:18:33.209 --> 01:18:35.628
- Where's the duck?
- Duck.

1070
01:18:35.794 --> 01:18:38.255
- Zebra.
- Zebra.

1071
01:18:38.422 --> 01:18:40.299
Zebra. Cat.

1072
01:18:40.466 --> 01:18:42.176
Duck.

1073
01:18:42.635 --> 01:18:44.094
Meow.

1074
01:18:44.261 --> 01:18:45.804
There's the pig.

1075
01:18:45.971 --> 01:18:48.140
Brooke Taylor's here again.

1076
01:18:48.307 --> 01:18:51.310
Aww. Maybe she'll be
pregnant this time.

1077
01:18:51.602 --> 01:18:53.520
I hope so.

1078
01:18:55.981 --> 01:18:59.109
- You ready, son?
- I can't find my cleats.

1079
01:18:59.276 --> 01:19:00.986
They're right here by the door.

1080
01:19:01.153 --> 01:19:03.155
Oh, thanks.

1081
01:19:06.200 --> 01:19:09.578
You realize you're playing for
the state championship tonight?

1082
01:19:09.745 --> 01:19:12.498
I don't know why I'm so nervous.
I'm not even gonna play.

1083
01:19:13.666 --> 01:19:15.459
You know I'm proud of you,
don't you?

1084
01:19:15.626 --> 01:19:16.669
Yes, sir.

1085
01:19:16.835 --> 01:19:19.546
Don't ever doubt it.
Whether you play or not...

1086
01:19:19.713 --> 01:19:21.257
...I'll be right there
praying for you.

1087
01:19:21.632 --> 01:19:22.675
Thanks, Dad.

1088
01:19:23.217 --> 01:19:25.970
Let's go pick a fight
with some giants.

1089
01:19:29.014 --> 01:19:31.308
Here's the results
for B. Taylor.

1090
01:19:31.475 --> 01:19:33.519
Oh, I'll take that.

1091
01:19:35.437 --> 01:19:36.563
Oh.

1092
01:19:36.730 --> 01:19:39.733
- Negative?
- Yes.

1093
01:20:45.382 --> 01:20:48.093
I will still love you, Lord.

1094
01:20:50.596 --> 01:20:53.390
I will still love you.

1095
01:22:16.557 --> 01:22:19.810
All right, God.
You got us here.

1096
01:22:20.394 --> 01:22:23.063
Whatever happens,
may you get the glory.

1097
01:22:24.857 --> 01:22:26.024
Phew.

1098
01:22:36.535 --> 01:22:38.036
Coach, what are you doing here?

1099
01:22:38.203 --> 01:22:40.205
You're at the state championship.
What do you think I'm doing here?

1100
01:22:40.372 --> 01:22:43.250
Any time a former player would get
this far, you know I'd be there.

1101
01:22:43.417 --> 01:22:46.336
- No, it blows me away.
- Well, how you feeling?

1102
01:22:47.880 --> 01:22:49.298
A little bit nervous.

1103
01:22:49.465 --> 01:22:52.050
This championship,
it's kind of surreal for me.

1104
01:22:52.217 --> 01:22:55.220
Yeah. Well, I can promise you, I don't care
what level of ball you're coaching...

1105
01:22:55.387 --> 01:22:58.182
...it's surreal when you make it
to the championship game.

1106
01:22:58.348 --> 01:23:01.477
And, Grant, I can just tell you, I'm so
proud of you and what you've done.

1107
01:23:01.643 --> 01:23:04.354
I've been reading about the team
and where you've gone.

1108
01:23:04.521 --> 01:23:05.689
And more than anything else...

1109
01:23:05.856 --> 01:23:08.692
...I'm just proud of the fact that you
finally learned how to win the big one.

1110
01:23:08.859 --> 01:23:09.902
We haven't played them yet.

1111
01:23:10.068 --> 01:23:12.362
You won the big one
when you accepted Christ.

1112
01:23:12.529 --> 01:23:15.407
And now, as you're teaching
these guys and minister to them...

1113
01:23:15.574 --> 01:23:17.159
...I think it's just fantastic.

1114
01:23:17.826 --> 01:23:20.496
I got it.
These players got it.

1115
01:23:20.662 --> 01:23:24.333
Well, I can promise you, win or lose
this game, you guys are champions.

1116
01:23:24.500 --> 01:23:26.585
- I appreciate that.
- But, hey, while you're here...

1117
01:23:26.752 --> 01:23:28.545
...you might as well win it, huh?

1118
01:23:28.712 --> 01:23:32.508
I'm gonna try my best. You know,
this team we're playing, they're huge.

1119
01:23:32.674 --> 01:23:36.011
They're fast, they're strong. I just
don't want my players to be afraid.

1120
01:23:36.178 --> 01:23:42.434
Well, in God's word, he said
365 different times, "Do not fear."

1121
01:23:42.601 --> 01:23:46.271
If he says it that many times, you know
he's serious about it, don't you?

1122
01:23:46.438 --> 01:23:48.774
I would guess so.
I needed to hear that.

1123
01:23:48.941 --> 01:23:51.610
Well, look, you're gonna do
great tonight. I know you're busy.

1124
01:23:51.777 --> 01:23:53.570
I'm gonna go up in those stands
and cheer you on.

1125
01:23:53.737 --> 01:23:55.447
- Good to see you.
- All right. God bless you, man.

1126
01:23:55.614 --> 01:23:57.241
Thanks, coach.

1127
01:24:14.716 --> 01:24:17.803
In about five minutes
we head out for the warm-up.

1128
01:24:17.970 --> 01:24:20.222
I wanna say two things.

1129
01:24:20.889 --> 01:24:23.141
Number one,
I love you and I'm proud of you.

1130
01:24:24.434 --> 01:24:27.396
I wouldn't trade this season
for anything in the world.

1131
01:24:28.313 --> 01:24:32.150
Secondly, you're about to play
the biggest team you've ever faced.

1132
01:24:32.317 --> 01:24:35.529
They're strong,
fast and undefeated.

1133
01:24:36.488 --> 01:24:38.156
So far.

1134
01:24:39.032 --> 01:24:41.952
But I want you to remember
where God has brought us.

1135
01:24:42.119 --> 01:24:44.746
I want you to remember
how hard you've worked.

1136
01:24:44.913 --> 01:24:48.750
We weren't supposed to have
a winning season, but we do.

1137
01:24:48.917 --> 01:24:52.004
We weren't supposed to advance
through the playoffs, but we did.

1138
01:24:52.754 --> 01:24:56.300
We're not supposed
to be here, but we are.

1139
01:24:56.550 --> 01:24:59.761
So if there's anything in you that says
this is a losing effort, throw it out.

1140
01:24:59.928 --> 01:25:03.098
Because as I stand here, I believe
that as long as we honor God...

1141
01:25:03.265 --> 01:25:05.517
...nothing is impossible.

1142
01:25:06.351 --> 01:25:08.145
Nothing.

1143
01:25:09.521 --> 01:25:14.651
Leave everything out on the field.
Give your best to God tonight.

1144
01:25:14.901 --> 01:25:19.573
And whether we leave the field the victors
or not, we will give God the glory.

1145
01:25:20.574 --> 01:25:22.075
Now...

1146
01:25:23.285 --> 01:25:25.662
...who will go fight
the Giants with me?

1147
01:25:52.856 --> 01:25:55.233
You've gotta be kidding me.

1148
01:26:13.168 --> 01:26:15.587
<i>The Giants elect
to receive after winning the coin toss.</i>

1149
01:26:15.754 --> 01:26:18.423
<i>We're just seconds away from the
state-championship football game.</i>

1150
01:26:18.590 --> 01:26:21.677
<i>Dale, I gotta tell you. It is impressive
that Shiloh has made it this far...</i>

1151
01:26:21.843 --> 01:26:24.429
...but the field tonight
really looks lopsided.

1152
01:26:24.596 --> 01:26:25.639
It definitely does.

1153
01:26:25.806 --> 01:26:28.308
I'm looking at 85 players
on the Richland sidelines...

1154
01:26:28.475 --> 01:26:30.435
<i>...as opposed to 32 for Shiloh.</i>

1155
01:26:30.602 --> 01:26:31.978
<i>Even if the Eagles had great talent...</i>

1156
01:26:32.145 --> 01:26:34.272
<i>...they can't bring in fresh players
like the Giants can.</i>

1157
01:26:34.481 --> 01:26:36.692
That's really gonna hurt them
in the second half.

1158
01:26:36.858 --> 01:26:38.360
All right.
Let's go, Joshua.

1159
01:26:41.780 --> 01:26:45.283
<i>The Eagles kick off and
the state championship game's underway.</i>

1160
01:26:45.450 --> 01:26:48.370
<i>Jerod House will receive the kick
and he'll head down the field.</i>

1161
01:26:48.537 --> 01:26:51.123
<i>He gets a couple blocks and breaks
outside. He's got some daylight.</i>

1162
01:26:51.289 --> 01:26:54.292
<i>But the Eagles will give chase and they'll
take him down around the 50-yard line.</i>

1163
01:26:54.459 --> 01:26:56.294
<i>And that's where the Giants
will set up shop tonight.</i>

1164
01:26:56.461 --> 01:27:00.424
First down and 10, in good field position
to start this state championship game.

1165
01:27:00.590 --> 01:27:02.884
Get up there. Brock,
watch them up the middle.

1166
01:27:03.051 --> 01:27:05.637
Come on. Let's go, boys.

1167
01:27:05.804 --> 01:27:09.057
<i>Wes Porter will call the play for
the Giants, and he steps back to pass.</i>

1168
01:27:09.224 --> 01:27:12.436
<i>He's got Damien Fuller streaking
down the sideline, and he lets it fly.</i>

1169
01:27:12.602 --> 01:27:15.897
<i>Fuller will take the pass in, he will
race into the end zone untouched.</i>

1170
01:27:16.064 --> 01:27:19.401
And the Giants strike early here
in the football game with the first score.

1171
01:27:19.568 --> 01:27:22.279
Welcome to
state-championship football.

1172
01:27:22.446 --> 01:27:23.989
Hey, man, this is
a whole new level.

1173
01:27:24.156 --> 01:27:25.198
They are quick off the line.

1174
01:27:25.365 --> 01:27:26.825
- We've gotta stay further back.
- I know. I'll adjust.

1175
01:27:27.159 --> 01:27:29.619
<i>The Eagles will start this drive
at the 19-yard line.</i>

1176
01:27:29.786 --> 01:27:32.748
<i>Zach Avery drops back to pass
and he passes to Jeremy Johnson.</i>

1177
01:27:32.914 --> 01:27:34.958
<i>But the pass is batted down
by the Giants.</i>

1178
01:27:35.125 --> 01:27:37.544
That's right.
That's the way we do it.

1179
01:27:37.711 --> 01:27:40.422
<i>Avery hands it to Jacob Hall,
who tries to run up the middle...</i>

1180
01:27:40.589 --> 01:27:44.009
<i>...but he gets absolutely nowhere
as he is swamped by defenders.</i>

1181
01:27:49.181 --> 01:27:51.850
Ten, 10, hit, hit.

1182
01:27:53.560 --> 01:27:55.479
<i>Eagles look to pass,
but here come the Giants.</i>

1183
01:27:55.645 --> 01:27:57.898
<i>And they're gonna get the sack.
And that's gonna force the Eagles...</i>

1184
01:27:58.064 --> 01:27:59.816
<i>...into a punting situation
on fourth down.</i>

1185
01:27:59.983 --> 01:28:04.029
Whoo! Baby, ain't that
pretty? Whoo!

1186
01:28:07.199 --> 01:28:10.202
<i>Jerod House will receive the kick
and he'll head down the field.</i>

1187
01:28:10.368 --> 01:28:13.914
<i>He gets a couple blocks and breaks
outside. He's got some daylight.</i>

1188
01:28:35.560 --> 01:28:37.979
Okay. All right, time...
Ref, timeout.

1189
01:28:39.147 --> 01:28:41.858
After gaining eight yards,
the Eagles give up another sack.

1190
01:28:42.025 --> 01:28:44.277
And they're gonna have to
punt it away on fourth down.

1191
01:28:44.444 --> 01:28:46.154
Dale, so far tonight
it's been all Richland.

1192
01:28:46.321 --> 01:28:48.281
Zach, that was my fault.
I should not have called that play.

1193
01:28:48.448 --> 01:28:49.991
Coach, they're all over us.
Nobody's open.

1194
01:28:50.158 --> 01:28:51.243
They're knocking us
around out there.

1195
01:28:51.409 --> 01:28:52.702
I know they are,
but they're getting cocky.

1196
01:28:52.869 --> 01:28:56.206
We cannot let them play their game.
Defense, I want you to blitz on first down.

1197
01:28:56.373 --> 01:28:58.041
We've gotta get them
off their rhythm. Let's go.

1198
01:29:25.527 --> 01:29:26.611
No!

1199
01:29:38.915 --> 01:29:42.002
Field-goal unit.
Let's go, let's go, let's go.

1200
01:29:42.168 --> 01:29:44.296
Good job. Good job.
Keep it up.

1201
01:29:44.462 --> 01:29:46.881
What universe are you in?
Get in the game.

1202
01:29:52.304 --> 01:29:54.472
<i>So with a few seconds left
in the first half...</i>

1203
01:29:54.639 --> 01:29:57.142
<i>...it looked as if the Giants were
gonna take a three-touchdown lead...</i>

1204
01:29:57.309 --> 01:30:00.812
...but after an Eagles interception,
we've got a 14 to 7 football game.

1205
01:30:06.234 --> 01:30:09.613
We can't keep running our normal plays,
man. Their defense is killing us.

1206
01:30:09.779 --> 01:30:14.159
I agree. We cannot outmuscle them
and we cannot outrun them.

1207
01:30:14.326 --> 01:30:16.244
We've gotta outsmart them.

1208
01:30:16.703 --> 01:30:18.038
Trick plays?

1209
01:30:18.204 --> 01:30:19.664
Just enough
to keep them guessing.

1210
01:30:19.831 --> 01:30:21.333
You see another way?

1211
01:30:21.499 --> 01:30:23.418
You just can't use them
too often, though.

1212
01:30:23.585 --> 01:30:24.919
They catch on, we toast.

1213
01:30:25.086 --> 01:30:27.339
We're toast anyway if we don't
put some points on that board.

1214
01:30:27.505 --> 01:30:31.009
We have gotta make it through the fourth
quarter. And they got a deep bench.

1215
01:30:32.010 --> 01:30:33.595
First of all,
we're still in this game.

1216
01:30:33.762 --> 01:30:35.972
Good job on the defense
getting us on the board.

1217
01:30:36.139 --> 01:30:38.266
I believe they thought
this would be a shutout.

1218
01:30:38.433 --> 01:30:39.976
We're gonna keep
surprising them.

1219
01:30:40.143 --> 01:30:43.104
You've figured out they've got
power and speed, they're big...

1220
01:30:43.271 --> 01:30:45.106
...but they're also predictable.

1221
01:30:45.273 --> 01:30:46.941
We have gotta stay together.

1222
01:30:47.984 --> 01:30:51.905
We can't outrun them,
but we can outsmart them.

1223
01:30:53.156 --> 01:30:56.951
<i>With the Giants leading the Eagles 14-7,
we get set to bring you the second half...</i>

1224
01:30:57.118 --> 01:30:58.662
<i>...of this state-championship
football game.</i>

1225
01:30:58.828 --> 01:31:02.499
<i>And unless the Eagles can find a way
to solve Richland's size and strength...</i>

1226
01:31:02.666 --> 01:31:06.544
...the Giants could very well be taking
their fourth consecutive state title tonight.

1227
01:31:11.633 --> 01:31:13.635
Make it work, Zach.

1228
01:31:19.557 --> 01:31:21.559
<i>And the Eagles come out
with a little trickery.</i>

1229
01:31:21.726 --> 01:31:24.396
<i>And they're just about to tie
this football game.</i>

1230
01:31:32.737 --> 01:31:35.490
Hustle, hustle. Come on.
Come on. Let's go. Let's go. Let's go.

1231
01:31:35.657 --> 01:31:38.243
Make them pay, boys.
Make them pay.

1232
01:31:44.332 --> 01:31:45.875
Come on.
That was dirty.

1233
01:31:49.295 --> 01:31:51.589
He's hurt. He's hurt. He's hurt.

1234
01:31:57.470 --> 01:31:59.597
<i>Joshua Webster's
being helped off the field...</i>

1235
01:31:59.764 --> 01:32:02.642
...with what we have been told up here
in the press box is a broken collarbone.

1236
01:32:02.809 --> 01:32:06.855
That came after a late hit by the Giants
after the Eagles tied the game at 14 apiece.

1237
01:32:07.021 --> 01:32:09.023
- Stupid. That was dirty.
- Hey, calm down.

1238
01:32:09.190 --> 01:32:11.609
This is a new ball game.
Joshua's gonna be all right.

1239
01:32:11.776 --> 01:32:15.029
David, come here.
You gotta cover for Joshua now.

1240
01:32:15.196 --> 01:32:16.948
- I need 110 percent, okay?
- All right, coach.

1241
01:32:17.115 --> 01:32:18.950
Be the man.
Kickoff team. Let's go.

1242
01:32:35.091 --> 01:32:36.760
Well, after a long drive,
the Giants score.

1243
01:32:36.926 --> 01:32:38.803
But the Eagles prevent
the two-point conversion...

1244
01:32:38.970 --> 01:32:41.055
<i>...leaving this
a 20 to 14 football game.</i>

1245
01:32:41.222 --> 01:32:42.849
Why are they even
on the scoreboard?

1246
01:32:43.016 --> 01:32:44.726
They shouldn't even
be in this game.

1247
01:32:44.893 --> 01:32:47.270
For the rest of your life,
you will remember today.

1248
01:32:47.437 --> 01:32:50.774
I want you to remember that you held
nothing back, you did not lose heart...

1249
01:32:50.940 --> 01:32:53.318
...you did not stop fighting,
you did not quit.

1250
01:32:53.485 --> 01:32:56.154
They're like little dogs
nipping at your heels.

1251
01:32:56.321 --> 01:32:58.490
Now get out there
and stomp them.

1252
01:33:02.660 --> 01:33:05.330
That's what I'm talking about.
That's my defense.

1253
01:33:07.832 --> 01:33:09.834
Let's go, Eagles.
He's going for a bomb.

1254
01:33:10.001 --> 01:33:14.005
Let's go. He's going for a bomb.
Don't get beat. Go.

1255
01:33:16.466 --> 01:33:19.385
<i>With seven minutes left on the clock, the
Eagles have shown the determination...</i>

1256
01:33:19.552 --> 01:33:21.179
...of a school twice their size.

1257
01:33:21.346 --> 01:33:26.184
The Giants will now attempt a 35-yard
field goal to extend their lead.

1258
01:33:28.603 --> 01:33:30.688
That is the last time
we go for a field goal.

1259
01:33:30.855 --> 01:33:33.233
We should be in the end zone
every stinking time.

1260
01:33:34.192 --> 01:33:37.362
Double flex wall.
Double flex wall.

1261
01:33:46.621 --> 01:33:48.540
And hit.

1262
01:33:53.461 --> 01:33:57.715
Go. Go. Go.

1263
01:34:03.304 --> 01:34:04.514
What are you doing?

1264
01:34:04.681 --> 01:34:06.349
Field-goal unit.
Go. Let's go. Let's go.

1265
01:34:06.516 --> 01:34:08.476
Field-goal unit.
Let's go.

1266
01:34:08.643 --> 01:34:10.728
- Good job. All right.
- That's my team.

1267
01:34:10.895 --> 01:34:14.232
Coach, I need a rest.
I can't go much more.

1268
01:34:14.399 --> 01:34:16.651
Brock, I need you on that field.
You have gotta stay in the game.

1269
01:34:16.818 --> 01:34:18.903
- I need you on the field.
- Yes, sir.

1270
01:34:19.070 --> 01:34:21.239
David Childers is in to kick
for Joshua Webster.

1271
01:34:21.406 --> 01:34:24.033
We understand that this is his
first season of football...

1272
01:34:24.200 --> 01:34:25.743
...and he's gone
three for four this season.

1273
01:34:25.910 --> 01:34:28.746
<i>And looking at the stats,
he's been limited to short-range kicks.</i>

1274
01:34:28.913 --> 01:34:31.833
Come on, David. You got this.

1275
01:34:50.727 --> 01:34:52.270
Yeah.

1276
01:34:57.066 --> 01:34:59.777
Timeout, ref. Ref, timeout.

1277
01:35:01.195 --> 01:35:04.949
Coach, I'm done.
Someone else has gotta lead.

1278
01:35:05.116 --> 01:35:08.119
Brock, this is when it matters most.
I know you're tired.

1279
01:35:08.286 --> 01:35:10.079
It's easy to lead
when you're strong.

1280
01:35:10.246 --> 01:35:12.123
But now is when you lead us,
right now.

1281
01:35:12.290 --> 01:35:15.877
Can you give me four more downs?
I just need four more downs.

1282
01:35:16.044 --> 01:35:18.212
Four more.

1283
01:35:18.379 --> 01:35:19.881
All right, come here. Come here.

1284
01:35:20.048 --> 01:35:23.259
This is our time and you've got
to put the nails in the coffin.

1285
01:35:23.426 --> 01:35:26.971
Look at me. Look at me. We didn't fight
this far to give up in the last quarter.

1286
01:35:27.138 --> 01:35:28.640
You've gotta leave
everything on the field.

1287
01:35:28.806 --> 01:35:31.059
And field goals,
they're not an option.

1288
01:35:31.225 --> 01:35:33.728
I need you for four more downs.
Who's with me?

1289
01:35:33.895 --> 01:35:35.813
Now get out there and get it done.

1290
01:35:35.980 --> 01:35:38.983
With less than two minutes left on
the clock, the Giants stand on the verge...

1291
01:35:39.150 --> 01:35:41.819
...of their fourth-straight
consecutive state title.

1292
01:35:41.986 --> 01:35:46.240
<i>A tired Eagles team lines up
to face them yet again.</i>

1293
01:35:48.952 --> 01:35:51.287
Stone wall. Stone wall.

1294
01:35:51.454 --> 01:35:53.665
Yes. Stone wall.

1295
01:35:53.831 --> 01:35:55.333
Stone wall.
Stone wall.

1296
01:35:55.500 --> 01:35:58.252
Stone wall. Stone wall.

1297
01:35:58.419 --> 01:36:00.171
<i>The Giants line up first and goal.</i>

1298
01:36:00.338 --> 01:36:02.590
<i>This score will solidify
the state championship.</i>

1299
01:36:02.757 --> 01:36:05.176
<i>Hand the ball off... No, wait
a minute. He is stopped.</i>

1300
01:36:05.343 --> 01:36:08.012
<i>The Eagles are still in it, they're still
showing strong determination...</i>

1301
01:36:08.179 --> 01:36:10.515
<i>- to fight this one out.</i>
- Three more downs.

1302
01:36:12.350 --> 01:36:15.019
- Three more.
- Yeah!

1303
01:36:15.186 --> 01:36:16.646
You gotta hang with me.

1304
01:36:16.813 --> 01:36:19.857
I know it's getting tough,
but we've gotta stop them right here.

1305
01:36:20.024 --> 01:36:22.360
It's second down
and goal to go for the Giants.

1306
01:36:22.527 --> 01:36:24.320
<i>The state title is within their grasp.</i>

1307
01:36:24.487 --> 01:36:28.241
<i>Both of the stands are on their feet
as they get ready to run this play.</i>

1308
01:36:28.408 --> 01:36:30.201
<i>Wes Porter will take it.
He's gonna try to run it.</i>

1309
01:36:30.368 --> 01:36:32.620
<i>No, the Eagles have
stopped him again.</i>

1310
01:36:32.787 --> 01:36:35.373
That's my team. That's my team.

1311
01:36:38.543 --> 01:36:40.712
Come on.
Get it in the end zone.

1312
01:36:40.878 --> 01:36:42.505
Two more.

1313
01:36:42.672 --> 01:36:45.633
<i>And here we go again.
They're gonna tee it up and try it again.</i>

1314
01:36:45.800 --> 01:36:48.803
<i>Wes Porter will take the snap.
He's looking to pass into the corner.</i>

1315
01:36:48.970 --> 01:36:51.806
<i>He's got somebody there.
But, no, the Eagles bat down the pass.</i>

1316
01:36:51.973 --> 01:36:53.891
<i>And the crowd is
going nuts right now.</i>

1317
01:36:54.058 --> 01:36:55.768
<i>The Giants have been kept out
of the end zone...</i>

1318
01:36:55.935 --> 01:36:57.395
<i>...by the Eagles
on three straight plays.</i>

1319
01:36:57.562 --> 01:37:00.189
And now Bobby Lee Duke
will have a big decision to make.

1320
01:37:00.356 --> 01:37:01.816
Coach, we have gotta
go for a field goal.

1321
01:37:01.983 --> 01:37:04.819
We are not going for a field goal.

1322
01:37:06.529 --> 01:37:11.743
He's not kicking it. Brock. Brock.
One more down. One more down.

1323
01:37:13.119 --> 01:37:15.913
<i>It's fourth down and the Giants
are going for the touchdown.</i>

1324
01:37:16.080 --> 01:37:18.708
This crowd is going
absolutely berserk right now.

1325
01:37:18.875 --> 01:37:20.501
<i>They line up at the one-yard line.</i>

1326
01:37:20.668 --> 01:37:22.587
<i>Wes Porter's gonna take the snap.
They're gonna run it.</i>

1327
01:37:22.754 --> 01:37:26.716
<i>Brock Kelley's gonna meet him head-on.
And there's a fumble. There's a fumble.</i>

1328
01:37:27.467 --> 01:37:30.386
<i>The Eagles have the football.
They're taking it back down the field.</i>

1329
01:37:30.553 --> 01:37:32.847
<i>He's at the 40. He's at the 50.</i>

1330
01:37:33.014 --> 01:37:36.309
He's at the 40. And he'll be run
out of bounds at the 34-yard line.

1331
01:37:36.476 --> 01:37:39.103
Are you believing this?
With two seconds left on the clock...

1332
01:37:39.270 --> 01:37:41.564
...the Eagles have got a shot
at this football game.

1333
01:37:47.612 --> 01:37:49.197
Two seconds, Grant.
We've got time for a Hail Mary.

1334
01:37:49.363 --> 01:37:50.990
No, no. The defense
is too strong for the pass.

1335
01:37:51.157 --> 01:37:53.743
No, we can't run it.
That's our only option.

1336
01:37:54.535 --> 01:37:55.745
You gotta kick it, man.

1337
01:37:57.830 --> 01:37:59.290
David.

1338
01:37:59.916 --> 01:38:01.209
I need a 51-yard field goal.

1339
01:38:01.375 --> 01:38:02.502
Coach, I can't kick that far.

1340
01:38:02.668 --> 01:38:04.462
David, they've been stopping
the run and the pass all night.

1341
01:38:04.629 --> 01:38:06.881
- You're my best option.
- Coach, the farthest I've ever kicked...

1342
01:38:07.048 --> 01:38:09.884
...is a 39-yarder. There is no way
I can kick a 51-yard field goal.

1343
01:38:10.051 --> 01:38:12.261
I believe you can. Your job
is to do the best you can...

1344
01:38:12.428 --> 01:38:14.722
...and leave the results up to God.
I need you on that field.

1345
01:38:14.889 --> 01:38:17.308
All right, field-goal unit.

1346
01:38:17.725 --> 01:38:20.478
Grant, we've gotta throw it.
He can't kick it from there. It's too far.

1347
01:38:20.645 --> 01:38:23.231
- No, it's not.
- What are you doing?

1348
01:38:23.397 --> 01:38:25.483
I'm preparing for rain.

1349
01:38:26.192 --> 01:38:28.653
I don't understand this,
but with two seconds left on the clock...

1350
01:38:28.820 --> 01:38:31.364
...Coach Grant Taylor and the Eagles
are putting the game in the hands...

1351
01:38:31.531 --> 01:38:33.241
...of a 145-pound
backup kicker.

1352
01:38:33.407 --> 01:38:35.409
<i>This is not
a good move on Grant Taylor's part.</i>

1353
01:38:35.576 --> 01:38:36.661
<i>He even has to kick into the wind.</i>

1354
01:38:40.331 --> 01:38:41.958
David.

1355
01:38:42.125 --> 01:38:43.960
David.

1356
01:38:45.670 --> 01:38:47.713
He's not ready, Grant.
He don't think he can do it.

1357
01:38:47.880 --> 01:38:51.801
I don't have any more timeouts.
Call a timeout, Bobby Lee.

1358
01:38:51.968 --> 01:38:55.012
- This kid can't kick that far.
- Call that timeout.

1359
01:38:55.179 --> 01:38:58.015
Call a timeout anyway
and let's ice him.

1360
01:39:03.271 --> 01:39:04.355
David, come here.

1361
01:39:06.149 --> 01:39:07.775
David, you're telling yourself
you're gonna miss this kick.

1362
01:39:07.942 --> 01:39:09.527
Coach, it's too far.

1363
01:39:09.694 --> 01:39:13.197
Listen to me. Do you think
God could help you make this kick?

1364
01:39:13.531 --> 01:39:16.033
- Do you believe it, David?
- Yeah, if he wants to.

1365
01:39:16.200 --> 01:39:19.078
So do I. But you have gotta give him
your best and leave the rest up to him.

1366
01:39:19.245 --> 01:39:21.205
Will you do that for me?

1367
01:39:29.964 --> 01:39:32.633
David, whether you make this field goal
or not, we're gonna praise him.

1368
01:39:32.800 --> 01:39:36.012
But don't you walk off this field
having done any less than your best.

1369
01:39:56.365 --> 01:39:58.409
- Can I help you?
- Don't touch me.

1370
01:39:58.576 --> 01:40:00.203
I'm standing for my son.

1371
01:40:03.331 --> 01:40:06.000
God, help me make this kick.

1372
01:40:11.839 --> 01:40:14.508
Kick it now. Kick it now.

1373
01:40:14.675 --> 01:40:16.385
Hit.

1374
01:40:24.060 --> 01:40:27.188
<i>The kick is up. It's on
its way. It's long enough. It's high enough.</i>

1375
01:40:27.355 --> 01:40:30.775
<i>Does it have the distance? It does.
It's good. It's good. It's good.</i>

1376
01:40:30.942 --> 01:40:32.985
<i>The Eagles have won. The Eagles
have won the state championship.</i>

1377
01:40:33.152 --> 01:40:34.278
Thank you, God.

1378
01:40:34.445 --> 01:40:38.282
<i>I can't believe what I've just seen.
I cannot believe what I've just seen.</i>

1379
01:40:38.449 --> 01:40:40.368
A miracle has occurred
here tonight.

1380
01:40:40.534 --> 01:40:44.747
<i>The Shiloh Eagles have defeated
the Richland Giants 24 to 23...</i>

1381
01:40:44.914 --> 01:40:47.875
...to take the state title
for the first time in their history.

1382
01:40:48.042 --> 01:40:50.962
<i>It's incredible.
It's absolutely unbelievable.</i>

1383
01:40:52.964 --> 01:40:56.133
You are a state champion.
You are a state champion.

1384
01:41:25.788 --> 01:41:29.250
All right.
Who's the state champions?

1385
01:41:36.966 --> 01:41:38.843
Okay. Okay.

1386
01:41:39.010 --> 01:41:40.970
I got something to say.

1387
01:41:41.846 --> 01:41:43.264
David Childers.

1388
01:41:48.352 --> 01:41:51.355
Don't you ever let anyone
tell you that you're under par...

1389
01:41:51.522 --> 01:41:53.858
...second-rate or inferior.

1390
01:41:55.693 --> 01:41:58.654
I just watched God
do a miracle through you.

1391
01:41:58.821 --> 01:42:04.201
I saw a field of Giants,
85 of them to be exact, fall in defeat.

1392
01:42:04.368 --> 01:42:06.579
Now you tell me what's
impossible with God.

1393
01:42:06.746 --> 01:42:08.039
Nothing, coach.

1394
01:42:10.458 --> 01:42:13.169
Zach, I just watched you
and the offense do...

1395
01:42:13.336 --> 01:42:15.046
...what they said
could not be done.

1396
01:42:15.212 --> 01:42:17.173
Now you tell me what's
impossible with God.

1397
01:42:17.340 --> 01:42:19.342
Nothing, coach.

1398
01:42:19.508 --> 01:42:22.887
Brock, how about it?
You built that stone wall, didn't you?

1399
01:42:23.054 --> 01:42:24.513
And it stood.

1400
01:42:24.680 --> 01:42:27.099
Now you tell me what's
impossible with God.

1401
01:42:27.266 --> 01:42:29.226
- Nothing, coach.
- How about it, Scott?

1402
01:42:29.393 --> 01:42:30.728
What's impossible with God?

1403
01:42:30.895 --> 01:42:32.021
- Nothing.
- Are you sure?

1404
01:42:32.188 --> 01:42:35.066
Because those Giants are big.
They outnumber us three to one.

1405
01:42:35.232 --> 01:42:37.485
Are you sure there's
nothing impossible with God?

1406
01:42:37.651 --> 01:42:39.403
I'm sure, coach.

1407
01:42:39.570 --> 01:42:41.989
How about it, Nathan?
What's impossible with God?

1408
01:42:42.156 --> 01:42:44.408
- Nothing, coach.
- Jonathan?

1409
01:42:44.575 --> 01:42:45.576
Nothing.

1410
01:42:45.743 --> 01:42:48.079
- Are you positive?
- Positive, coach.

1411
01:42:48.245 --> 01:42:51.749
So am I. So am I.

1412
01:42:51.916 --> 01:42:54.794
God can do whatever he wants to do,
however he wants to do it.

1413
01:42:54.960 --> 01:42:57.630
And he chooses to work in our lives
because he loves us...

1414
01:42:57.797 --> 01:42:58.839
...because he's good.

1415
01:43:00.049 --> 01:43:04.720
Hope today's a milestone for what
he can do for the rest of your life...

1416
01:43:04.887 --> 01:43:06.597
...if you trust him.

1417
01:43:07.390 --> 01:43:09.934
Why don't we spend some time
thanking him?

1418
01:43:27.284 --> 01:43:30.037
Well, look who just
walked in this house.

1419
01:43:30.454 --> 01:43:33.999
Couldn't be the state-champion
coach Grant Taylor, could it?

1420
01:43:34.166 --> 01:43:36.710
Because he's not
supposed to live here.

1421
01:43:36.877 --> 01:43:38.879
He's supposed to be out
looking for a job.

1422
01:43:40.506 --> 01:43:42.425
God did it, Brooke.

1423
01:43:44.176 --> 01:43:45.719
He did it.

1424
01:43:48.764 --> 01:43:50.141
He gave me this job...

1425
01:43:52.685 --> 01:43:55.271
...provided for our needs...

1426
01:43:55.438 --> 01:43:57.440
...took away my fear.

1427
01:43:59.066 --> 01:44:02.236
He throws in the state championship
just because he can.

1428
01:44:08.159 --> 01:44:10.786
It's been one of
the best days of my life.

1429
01:44:11.537 --> 01:44:15.666
- The day's not over yet.
- What do you mean?

1430
01:44:16.959 --> 01:44:22.506
Grant Taylor, I just want you to
know that you've made the team.

1431
01:44:23.674 --> 01:44:25.342
What team?

1432
01:44:28.053 --> 01:44:30.222
The daddy team.

1433
01:44:33.559 --> 01:44:35.561
We're gonna have a baby?

1434
01:44:35.728 --> 01:44:38.522
We're gonna have a baby.

1435
01:44:45.988 --> 01:44:48.491
You tell me, Coach Taylor...

1436
01:44:48.657 --> 01:44:53.829
...tell me what's impossible
when God's on your side?

1437
01:44:56.207 --> 01:44:59.877
Oh, God. Oh, God.
I'm overwhelmed.
